{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick","id":1123364,"title":"The Problem with Flexible Magick","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-01T01:49:34-07:00","id":1123364,"title":"The Problem with Flexible Magick","content":"So in Mage you aren't just throwing around the kind of &quot;rotes&quot; that other Splats are stuck with. A Vampire uses Lure of Flames 5, and gets a very specific result using completely static rules.<br /> <br /> Mages, on the other hand, can do things their own way. You could set someone on fire, turn them into fire, teleport them into an umbral realm made entirely of the very concept of fire... if you have the Spheres, successes and bravery to do it (and face the consequences). This is cool in that it allows for truly Magickal events... but the problems start to pop up with Mechanics.<br /> <br /> Now Mage does have a lot of mechanical guidelines for damage, duration, range etc. but there are still problems. You can happily say that X Successes = Y Damage with a Forces effect, but many changes simply don't work that way. Turning someone's clothing into stone? How many successes are we talking? The ST could say anything from 3 to 5 I believe, depending on how they feel. Making the floor beneath someone into a liquid? Again, it's impressive, but the successes needed will vary.<br /> <br /> So it's not that Mage *lacks* rules, it's that the ST is forced to make decisions constantly and their opinions will vary from session to session, ST to ST, player to player. This isn't a bug, I'm guessing it's a feature.<br /> <br /> The problems arise when you realise that we have rules so that the ST's feelings don't shape the game too heavily. Implicitly or explicitly we have biases when it comes to our players and their actions. We'll feel differently to a player saying &quot;I attempt to use Spirit and Prime to erase the Nexus Crawler from existence... basically I call upon God's aid in smiting this monstrosity and casting it out of his creation&quot; than we'll feel when they say the same about a major NPC (or PC, but we'll get to that). Once it's someone we're invested in, we're more likely to um and ah and increase the successes needed, factor in the protections they have... see the problem here? PvP makes this into a NIGHTMARE. Luckily most of these effects where mechanics get blurry are going to be paradox-heavy, but that isn't going to matter while the scene is playing out, especially if one player is keen on eradicating the other for some reason.<br /> <br /> So, basically... have I missed something? Is this a legitimate problem you run into as STs and Players? I've only done a one-shot with a single player so my experience is limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T01:59:10-07:00","id":1123368,"title":"","content":"For me it is important to make clear that if you want to kill(take out of the game) someone, you'll need 4 successes at minimum (3 with Forces).<br /> <br /> Otherwise there would be an abundance of heart attacks...<br /> <br /> The table feats of magick is your friend otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T02:00:23-07:00","id":1123369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123368#post1123368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me it is important to make clear that if you want to kill(take out of the game) someone, you'll need 4 successes at minimum (3 with Forces).<br /> <br /> Otherwise there would be an abundance of heart attacks...<br /> <br /> The table feats of magick is your friend otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what about people cheesing it with Correspondence? I mean nothing to stop you from working that heart attack into a Correspondence effect, correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T05:26:08-07:00","id":1123411,"title":"","content":"Sure.<br /> You'll need Life 3 / Correspondence 3 and at least 6 successes (4 for 8 levels of agg and 2 to 6 for the Correspondence bit depending on familiarity).<br /> <br /> So albeit possible for a starting level mage you look at an average of 8 successes without calculating defense of the target.<br /> <br /> So, yes a mage can kill mortals with impunity. Another Mage? Questionable.<br /> Another splat? Most likely not as a starting level mage (for vampires you need additional Matter, for werewolves Spirit, and so on)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T05:26:52-07:00","id":1123415,"title":"","content":"Nope. Correspondence makes anyone not protected by wards (meaning most Mages most of the time) vulnerable. However, it better work on the first try because if your target has Correspondence as well you will be in for retaliation.<br /> <br /> If this is a problem in your game it's can be easily dealt with, especially for &quot;death&quot; type effects. To outrightkill with magic effects, even heart attacks, the total heathlevels must be overcome (for balance sake at the very least) this will require at least 3 successes with Forces and 1 more for other spheres. This is in addition to successes needed for Corespondece range. This usually will require at least an extended roll. The target will be allowed an Awareness Roll (8 or higher) to notice magic being used against him as soon as the effect begins, giving a chance for defense. It may not seem like much but it's always been enough to discourage it in my games.<br /> <br /> Also if your players like this sort of tactic see how they like it used on them. That should cure the problem almost immediately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T05:41:53-07:00","id":1123420,"title":"","content":"OP, as you said, that's more feature than bug. When I join a mage game I am very careful with those things, either as ST or Player. Some are too restrictive, some are too loose, I adapt to what I can, and expect the same from others. With persistent groups consistency will be found.<br /> <br /> <br /> Where I feel I have to make things on the fly I write my own guidelines as the result shows itself conducive to the game.<br /> <br /> To determine base successes, for example, when it's about killing someone I prefer to require successes as I would with damage.<br /> Someone might complain &quot;But then I can't kill a small city making an impromptu reactor meltdown transmuting a liter of water into a liter of Plutonium-240 with some 8 successes&quot;<br /> To whom I reply &quot;Good&quot; and carry on. The damage mechanics of Mage are quite strong on their own already. You don't need to escape the &quot;2 dmg per sux on pure damage effects&quot; base to make nastier effects. Trivial opponents get blasted anyway, nasty opponents can be laid low with as little as a friction curse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123415#post1123415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Correspondence makes anyone not protected by wards (meaning most Mages most of the time) vulnerable. However, it better work on the first try because if your target has Correspondence as well you will be in for retaliation.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good one to do here is Countermagick. Countermagick has the same &quot;action space&quot; as defense rolls. I'm absolutely fine with letting a splat use countermagick (or their analog, usually some supernatural resistance thingie based on their power attributes) upon being sniped with correspondence.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 08-01-2017, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T05:43:34-07:00","id":1123421,"title":"","content":"But the problem for me is that with some Quintessence, an Ability roll to reduce difficulty, a sample of your target to make Correspondence easier, Willpower spent to guarantee successes... if you REALLY max out the roll you can kill basically anyone who isn't warded in a few rolls with Arete 2 or 3. And all the changes you need to make to make the roll easier? They're not a MASSIVE deal, really, a few points of Quintessence and Willpower aren't that serious, and something as simple as having one of their possessions can make it even easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T05:45:20-07:00","id":1123423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123420#post1123420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OP, as you said, that's more feature than bug. When I join a mage game I am very careful with those things, either as ST or Player. Some are too restrictive, some are too loose, I adapt to what I can, and expect the same from others. With persistent groups consistency will be found.<br /> <br /> <br /> Where I feel I have to make things on the fly I write my own guidelines as the result shows itself conducive to the game.<br /> <br /> To determine base successes, for example, when it's about killing someone I prefer to require successes as I would with damage.<br /> Someone might complain &quot;But then I can't kill a small city making an impromptu reactor meltdown transmuting a liter of water into a liter of Plutonium-240 with some 8 successes&quot;<br /> To whom I reply &quot;Good&quot; and carry on. The damage mechanics of Mage are quite strong on their own already. You don't need to escape the &quot;2 dmg per sux on pure damage effects&quot; base to make nastier effects. Trivial opponents get blasted anyway, nasty opponents can be laid low with as little as a friction curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but you'd let the Mage kill a city if they successfully infiltrated a nuclear power plant and caused a meltdown I'm assuming? I mean let's say it's a sandbox story with no narrative and &quot;I destroy the city&quot; is fair play from day one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T05:55:47-07:00","id":1123426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123369#post1123369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But what about people cheesing it with Correspondence? I mean nothing to stop you from working that heart attack into a Correspondence effect, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's stated in the 1st edition Mage: The Ascension Corebook, in the description of the Correspondence Sphere: &quot;Mages who persevere through the study of Correspondence gain knowledge that, when it is combined with other magickal Spheres, makes it so the Mistress or Master of Correspondence is unassailable.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ( Not identical to the original quote - the sentence in the book is incorrectly written, and I filled in the sentence with the words &quot;when&quot; and &quot;makes it so&quot;.<br /> Also added &quot;Mistress&quot;. )<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not really cheesing I'd say; though if it feels and/or is like it I'd house rule, among other things, the need to collect items - and perhaps specific items depending on what you want to cast - to provide the Correspondence link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:00:33-07:00","id":1123427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123426#post1123426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really cheesing I'd say; though if it feels and/or is like it I'd house rule, among other things, the need to collect items - and perhaps specific items depending on what you want to cast - to provide the Correspondence link.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I like this house-rule in theory, I think that it's a difficulty break not a prerequisite for a reason. Having a tuft of their hair, or their blood... it's nice, sure, but a Technomancer CAN just change the value HeartBeating=1 to HeartBeating=0 (as a flippant oversimplification) and having &quot;I need a sample of their blood&quot; as a prerequisite for a hacker would be... odd. And if the prerequisites vary by Paradigm (hair, blood, his Facebook profile picture) then that variety will be a source of imbalance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:05:53-07:00","id":1123430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123423#post1123423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, but you'd let the Mage kill a city if they successfully infiltrated a nuclear power plant and caused a meltdown I'm assuming? I mean let's say it's a sandbox story with no narrative and &quot;I destroy the city&quot; is fair play from day one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Working with the world is an excellent way of cutting magickal expenses.<br /> A &quot;less absurd&quot; example could be a car chase. An effect to make the tires slippery will be far more simple than any damage effect that'd deal as much damage as a high-speed collision. A well prepared mage can probably pull that off with a diff 3 or 4 roll requiring 3~ successes on a standard car.<br /> Heck, another might pre-cast a buff to give himself a huge edge driving his own car on the chase, making it relatively easy to bump into other cars just the right way to crash them. That's another efficient use or magick for spreading death and mayhem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 08-01-2017, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:15:12-07:00","id":1123434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123430#post1123430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. Working with the world is an excellent way of cutting magickal expenses.<br /> A &quot;less absurd&quot; example could be a car chase. An effect to make the tires slippery will be far more simple than any damage effect that'd deal as much damage as a high-speed collision. A well prepared mage can probably pull that off with a diff 3 or 4 roll requiring 3~ successes on a standard car.<br /> Heck, another might pre-cast a buff to give himself a huge edge driving his own car on the chase, making it relatively easy to bump into other cars just the right way to crash them. That's another efficient use or magick for spreading death and mayhem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Correspondance + Forces to make a TINY, minute spark inside the fuel tank... I can't imagine that needing more than 2 successes total? The car is right in front of you, and the spark you're creating isn't even enough to do damage (on its own).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:17:02-07:00","id":1123437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123427#post1123427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I like this house-rule in theory, I think that it's a difficulty break not a prerequisite for a reason. Having a tuft of their hair, or their blood... it's nice, sure, but a Technomancer CAN just change the value HeartBeating=1 to HeartBeating=0 (as a flippant oversimplification) and having &quot;I need a sample of their blood&quot; as a prerequisite for a hacker would be... odd. And if the prerequisites vary by Paradigm (hair, blood, his Facebook profile picture) then that variety will be a source of imbalance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your virtualist definitely won't collect hair samples to work his correspondence. He might need to connect to a device that is very near him, though. A dashcam with the victim in its sights makes an okay link. A superuser connection to his cellphone while he's carrying it would be very strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 08-01-2017, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:19:52-07:00","id":1123439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123434#post1123434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or Correspondance + Forces to make a TINY, minute spark inside the fuel tank... I can't imagine that needing more than 2 successes total? The car is right in front of you, and the spark you're creating isn't even enough to do damage (on its own).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's useful to think of Patterns here. To get to someone's heart you have to get through that someone first. The same would apply to any structure in a car. It's a fuzzy line to draw, but in general the dice don't skip the whole to target the bit.<br /> <br /> For your fuel explosion I'd make it a &quot;ignite fuel on car&quot; effect. 2 successes (1 to target stuff, 1 for a very simple and small effect).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 08-01-2017, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:29:54-07:00","id":1123442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123439#post1123439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's useful to think of Patterns here. To get to someone's heart you have to get through that someone first. The same would apply to any structure in a car. It's a fuzzy line to draw, but in general the dice don't skip the whole to target the bit.<br /> <br /> For your fuel explosion I'd make it a &quot;ignite fuel on car&quot; effect. 2 successes (1 to target stuff, 1 for a very simple and small effect).</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that patterns are pretty important, so teleporting yourself *inside* someone else to &quot;explode&quot; them isn't okay, and teleporting their head off of their neck isn't okay... thankfully. I mean turning Vampires into Lawn Chairs is one thing, but removing the heads of Vampires from 50 miles away would be a bit too much.<br /> <br /> Does it matter if you know where the fuel tank is? You could add an extra success for *finding* the fuel tank (another case of needing Correspondence), or you can skip this with a Perception + Crafts (Mechanics) roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:30:49-07:00","id":1123444,"title":"","content":"Similar &quot;the consequences of this effect are greater than the successes might imply&quot; power over living beings does exist in a cognitive sense for us, if not in a mechanical sense for the system. Causing a pang of pain, a sudden urge, striking thirst or their like won't require much. A &quot;poke the heart&quot; effect would just induce fatigue or pain. &quot;Poke her pineal gland&quot; will probably just induce a period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:34:27-07:00","id":1123445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123444#post1123444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar &quot;the consequences of this effect are greater than the successes might imply&quot; power over living beings does exist in a cognitive sense for us, if not in a mechanical sense for the system. Causing a pang of pain, a sudden urge, striking thirst or their like won't require much. A &quot;poke the heart&quot; effect would just induce fatigue or pain. &quot;Poke her pineal gland&quot; will probably just induce a period.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean you could just use Mind from afar to make someone THINK they're having a heart attack... it won't kill them, but it will disable them pretty effectively.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Mind, I'm confused about Consensual stuff RE mind control. I mean can't you make ANYTHING consensual with mind?<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh he would think the Dinosaur is weird but before I conjured it I used Mind to make him think Dinosaurs are normal fauna.&quot; (hmm, so that's Prime to make the matter and energy out of nowhere, Life to make a living Dinosaur, Mind to give it thoughts and instincts... to be honest I doubt there are many Mages who can make Dinosaurs out of nowhere... Time + Correspondence would work perfectly though, but reaching back to the Jurassic Period would be tricky)<br /> <br /> &quot;Well I know that I'm a tentacle monster right now but I'm using Mind to make him see me as my normal form.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously you're needing more successes and a Botch would mean a HUGE Paradox backlash, but isn't it a cheat out of breaking the Consensus in many cases?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-01-2017, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:34:42-07:00","id":1123446,"title":"","content":"Also don't look too hard at correspondence if you're scared of the hax factor XD conjunctional correspondence is ONLY about the hax factor. It should never be easier than just being there doing the effect (mechanically represented by &quot;have this much Correspondence&quot; and &quot;add this many successes to the roll&quot;).<br /> <br /> The best you can do is just making it resistable as it'd be on an ambush or something. Allowing resistance is the big aide here. Countermagick and their analogues. Wards and protections should be far more effective and compound on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:41:03-07:00","id":1123449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123445#post1123445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean you could just use Mind from afar to make someone THINK they're having a heart attack... it won't kill them, but it will disable them pretty effectively.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Mind, I'm confused about Consensual stuff RE mind control. I mean can't you make ANYTHING consensual with mind?<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh he would think the Dinosaur is weird but before I conjured it I used Mind to make him think Dinosaurs are normal fauna.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well I know that I'm a tentacle monster right now but I'm using Mind to make him see me as my normal form.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously you're needing more successes and a Botch would mean a HUGE Paradox backlash, but isn't it a cheat out of breaking the Consensus in many cases?</div> </div> </div> </div>The morals and intricacies of consent will be up to you to determine, and can be as complicated as they can be easy, really. Since we don't have much of a real world analogue to the Mind sphere it can be hard XD<br /> <br /> Proper persuasion and setup can make someone want something they wouldn't in other contexts, no magick involved. The rights and wrongs of building that context are a separate matter. Is it wrong because the persuader deliberately built the proper context? is it not wrong if the persuader set the context by accident?<br /> With magick, execution is a big deal. Someone that good a smooth talker and someone roofying up his drink will easily be casting the same effect, mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:42:51-07:00","id":1123452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123449#post1123449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The morals and intricacies of consent will be up to you to determine, and can be as complicated as they can be easy, really. Since we don't have much of a real world analogue to the Mind sphere it can be hard XD<br /> <br /> Proper persuasion and setup can make someone want something they wouldn't in other contexts, no magick involved. The rights and wrongs of building that context are a separate matter. Is it wrong because the persuader deliberately built the proper context? is it not wrong if the persuader set the context by accident?<br /> With magick, execution is a big deal. Someone that good a smooth talker and someone roofying up his drink will easily be casting the same effect, mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>By Consensual I mean &quot;fits into the Consensus&quot;, not &quot;you have legitimate consent&quot;. Let's avoid THAT topic... I mean a good thread could be made around that but PLEASE let's not touch that here. Also, as a medical student I can confirm that the effects of rohypnol aren't really equivalent to being charming, at all. The symptoms of flunitrazepam are quite specific and don't really match the outcome of flirting, let's leave it at that :P<br /> <br /> So I mean &quot;with Mind can't you make anything, no matter how wacky, fit the local consensus?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-01-2017, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:47:13-07:00","id":1123453,"title":"","content":"XD Coincidence then, not consensuality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:47:49-07:00","id":1123454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123453#post1123453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">XD Coincidence then, not consensuality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah there you go... to be fair &quot;consensus&quot; and &quot;consensual&quot; have the same roots linguistically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:50:43-07:00","id":1123456,"title":"","content":"An effect generally doesn't change between coincidental and vulgar unless the impossibility's blatancy can be hidden/exposed.<br /> An impossible phenomenon that &quot;no one would see even if he was looking&quot; will usually be coincidental. For example, conjuring a small item from your pocket. An onlooker would just see you producing something from your pocket.<br /> <br /> YOU know it's a teleport, but &quot;reality&quot; just saw you pull a business card.<br /> If you're in a context where your pockets are more exposed (a scene where your pockets were checked by other people, like a patdown), would make it vulgar, for it was &quot;a known thing&quot; that your pockets were empty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:51:02-07:00","id":1123457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123427#post1123427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I like this house-rule in theory, I think that it's a difficulty break not a prerequisite for a reason. Having a tuft of their hair, or their blood... it's nice, sure, but a Technomancer CAN just change the value HeartBeating=1 to HeartBeating=0 (as a flippant oversimplification) and having &quot;I need a sample of their blood&quot; as a prerequisite for a hacker would be... odd. And if the prerequisites vary by Paradigm (hair, blood, his Facebook profile picture) then that variety will be a source of imbalance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not neccesirely.<br /> What you wrote about is something I think about often, and frankly it's not at all discussed in Mage: the Ascension books - that is, Paradigm-based increased effectiveness in certain situations. (It is implied in the way the Foundation and Pillar True Mages work in the rules. Some Foundations and Pillars, and some Pillars, do get - sometimes significantly - greater effects of their True Magick in regards to specific, appropriate goals and situations. Some True Magick Effects are easier to perform for some Foundation and Pillars Paradigms.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123427#post1123427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technomancer CAN just change the value HeartBeating=1 to HeartBeating=0 (as a flippant oversimplification)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you state yourself that this is a &quot;flippant oversimplification&quot;, why give it as an example at all? It's not that simple.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123427#post1123427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and having &quot;I need a sample of their blood&quot; as a prerequisite for a hacker would be... odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? If their True Magick works this way - why would it be odd? Do you think Technomancers have to do everything the 'techy' and 'XXI century' way, with everything coming down to social media and smartphones?<br /> Also, do you think they gain some major advantage(s) over Mystics in regards to their True Magick, in that it is somehow much easier?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123427#post1123427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if the prerequisites vary by Paradigm (hair, blood, his Facebook profile picture) then that variety will be a source of imbalance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you implying that the imbalance would be that the Technomancer's Paradigm would have an advantage over a Mystic's? If so, did you think that the Technomancer cannot target somebody who doesn't have a Facebook account? Or that maybe they will sooner or later find out that they also can't target somebody who visits their Facebook once or twice - or less - per week? ;-)<br /> <br /> <br /> The Correspondence link I would suggest here would not be a Facebook profile picture, but an extended conversation over Facebook - to the point of the target person(s) accepting - and downloading it through Facebook chat - a file from the Technomancer (and possibly also sending a personal file to the Technomancer, also over Facebook chat.)<br /> As I see it, if you want to get to your target person, targeting their Facebook account is not enough - as it exists on Facebook; it is a major step removed from the target from a Technomantic perspective, as compared to the files, operating system and contents that are on the target person's personal PC. You can target a person <i>through</i> their Facebook account, but it does require effort, work - and possibly entails risk - comparable to what a Mystic user of Correspondence (or the equivalent Pillar(s) for a Foundation and Pillars True Mage.) has to do.<br /> Do you still think there is some 'imbalance'? (How would you define this imbalance, by the way?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-01-2017, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:51:47-07:00","id":1123459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123456#post1123456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An effect generally doesn't change between coincidental and vulgar unless the impossibility's blatancy can be hidden/exposed.<br /> An impossible phenomenon that &quot;no one would see even if he was looking&quot; will usually be coincidental. For example, conjuring a small item from your pocket. An onlooker would just see you producing something from your pocket.<br /> <br /> YOU know it's a teleport, but &quot;reality&quot; just saw you pull a business card.<br /> If you're in a context where your pockets are more exposed (a scene where your pockets were checked by other people, like a patdown), would make it vulgar, for it was &quot;a known thing&quot; that your pockets were empty.</div> </div> </div> </div>However you can push it one step further; claim that you're skilled in conjuring tricks and you *might* still make it coincidental, correct?<br /> <br /> So we could talk about the Invisible Pink Orb in the room and say that conjuring it is 100% coincidental since no one can see it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:55:23-07:00","id":1123463,"title":"","content":"Therefore messing with someone's perceptions won't usually touch on coincidence. It might remove witnesses, which is already something.<br /> <br /> If you make that in a grander scale, however, things start to change. The Consensus is localized. Long term changes usually can be very effective. The key here is long term and little interference.<br /> Just like how your sanctum favors your Focus, you know? Spend the better part of a year convincing a small town that Slenderman exists, don't let newcomers linger, and you might be able Slender it up coincidentally.<br /> <br /> Now I'm imagining what would become vulgar by convincing a whole town that Texas doesn't exist...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123459#post1123459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However you can push it one step further; claim that you're skilled in conjuring tricks and you *might* still make it coincidental, correct?<br /> <br /> So we could talk about the Invisible Pink Orb in the room and say that conjuring it is 100% coincidental since no one can see it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, just don't forget some things are always vulgar (I'll conjure up the sample list later from M20). In a context where people would totally expect you to teleport you can teleport coincidentally. Magic shows! Wuxia moves in a hollywood studio or a remote tibetan temple! Exploding helicopters in Rio de Janeiro!<br /> <br /> Your invisible pink orb that is just there being an invisible pink orb? Yeah I'd call it coincidental. Nothing impossible is evident to anyone there. Start making it do stuff and we will rediscuss <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That's part of why perceptive magick is so strong...it's very rare for it to be vulgar!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 08-01-2017, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T06:56:19-07:00","id":1123465,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3254_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3254\" data-vbnamecard=\"3254\">Muad'Dib</a> Just saying that if you had prerequisites for inflicting harm via Correspondence, rather than making &quot;personal items&quot; an optional thing that gives a difficulty break, it would be difficult to provide a prerequisite that felt thematically appropriate for every Paradigm... and if you go for lots of different ones or give a general descriptor, some paradigms will have it easier than others. It doesn't have to be tech-based, it could be that Hermetics have it easier for example, my point is just that it would be hard to make the difficulty consistent across the different types of Magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T07:02:31-07:00","id":1123467,"title":"","content":"See now all I can see is a Correspondence 3, Mind 3 Illusionist who sits in their house and screws with other Supernaturals for fun.<br /> <br /> &quot;See, I managed to get the Vampires in my city to set up two separate Camarilla courts, being unaware of the other. Then I made them perceive eachother as Sabbat and watched the fireworks... what do you mean I'm wasting my talents?!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T07:26:03-07:00","id":1123481,"title":"","content":"That's some serious high level shenanigans <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T07:26:26-07:00","id":1123482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123467#post1123467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See now all I can see is a Correspondence 3, Mind 3 Illusionist who sits in their house and screws with other Supernaturals for fun.<br /> <br /> &quot;See, I managed to get the Vampires in my city to set up two separate Camarilla courts, being unaware of the other. Then I made them perceive eachother as Sabbat and watched the fireworks... what do you mean I'm wasting my talents?!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>He doesn't have time. SOmething with a &quot;Go first Power&quot; kills him while he's in the bathroom. What do you mean my KJ with principle of motion is wasting his time running around killing mages who don't have time? Apparently if I don't do this they will just sit in their room and work on mind and correspondence do mess with us. So premptively kill all mages!<br /> <br /> Replace this with Spirit of the Fray for Werewolves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T07:40:00-07:00","id":1123486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123465#post1123465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3254_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3254\" data-vbnamecard=\"3254\">Muad'Dib</a> Just saying that if you had prerequisites for inflicting harm via Correspondence, rather than making &quot;personal items&quot; an optional thing that gives a difficulty break, it would be difficult to provide a prerequisite that felt thematically appropriate for every Paradigm...</div> </div> </div> </div>Why and how would it be difficult?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123465#post1123465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and if you go for lots of different ones or give a general descriptor, some paradigms will have it easier than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by this - &quot;some paradigms will have it easier than others&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T07:44:32-07:00","id":1123488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123486#post1123486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why and how would it be difficult?<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you mean by this - &quot;some paradigms will have it easier than others&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay say that to give a heart attack you need to have someone's blood on you. For many, many paradigms this works perfectly, the blood being the key to someone's vitality. However for someone who believes that all of reality is an illusion, or someone who thinks that reality is one big computer program, or someone who thinks that reality is one big machine &quot;you need someone's blood&quot; feels weirdly restrictive and unthematic. Part of what's nice about Mage is everyone doing the same stuff in a totally different way, from killing someone with a pin through a doll's heart to killing someone through manipulating probability to create a deadly mugging to killing someone by smiting them and erasing their pattern entirely. What's nice, however, if that they are all bound by the same rules, even if the incidental details do vary (and the players are choosing to use different mechanics, though they do all have access to the same rolls if they so choose).<br /> <br /> Well imagine you gave each Paradigm a specific type of connection they need to kill someone from afar. Imagine one had blood, another had hair, and another had their True Name, hypothetically. Those three things vary greatly in how difficult they would be to acquire, and picking a list of things that are of vaguely equivalent difficulty isn't going to be a simple task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-01-2017, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T09:44:15-07:00","id":1123527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">See now all I can see is a Correspondence 3, Mind 3 Illusionist who sits in their house and screws with other Supernaturals for fun.</span> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">&quot;See, I managed to get the Vampires in my city to set up two separate Camarilla courts, being unaware of the other. Then I made them perceive eachother as Sabbat and watched the fireworks... what do you mean I'm wasting my talents?!<br /> </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> This isn't easy...but I see your point.<br /> <br /> It isn't easy because your mage has to:<br /> * Know about the Sabbat and the Camarilla, be aware of the existence of vampires that aren't aware of each other (if they are the shenanigan can still be made, but there may be resistences and increases on difficulties involved)<br /> * Have Correspondence links with all the vampires involved (I assume inteligent vampires do not leave a ot of data about themselves, nor like to be stalked to get their hair or pictures)<br /> * Cast a spell with enough successes to target all vampires and alter their perceptions for a long time<br /> <br /> But your point it's easy to understand: It's hard to defend yourself against this kind of shenanigans. Other supernaturals haven't a good defense against this kind of Shenanigans. Countermagick doesn't help much because with a ritual you can always get extra successes to surpass any resistence. Mages fare better because there isn't a clear limit on how much successes you can put into a defense to prevent Correspondence (and powerful mages may create &quot;retaliatory&quot; defenses that detect the attempt and do something to kill the mage that's on the other end), </span>they can detect and cut Correspondence link, and they have reasons to expect this kind of attack<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">.<br /> <br /> The best defense against Correspondence (not involving having Correspondence) it's to not give away your location nor information about you. Mages can't attack what they can't detect.</span><br /> </span><br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T09:52:19-07:00","id":1123531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">some paradigms will have it easier than others&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is a thing in Mage: For a Scientist, to heal you requires to have Medicine and expensive tools, for a faithful person, it's just a mater of praying (I don't need to know Theology, I don't believe in organized religion and don't care much for their &quot;lore&quot;).<br /> <br /> But this isn't much of a problem: If you're a scientist you're likely to have the resources and know-how you need as part of your character development, and hey!, it's likely to be more coincident to heal a wound with stitches than with a random prayer done without knowing proper christian rituals.<br /> <br /> With the &quot;Correspondence table&quot; isn't different, a Hermetic needs to research your True Name, an Orphan may find any of your natural name/s to be enough of a connection. Again, this isn't terrible, If you let random mages to know your name, it's your fault, and the Hermetic will have to research a little more, but he's Hermetic, he knows how to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-01-2017, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T10:14:17-07:00","id":1123536,"title":"","content":"There's also the big question: why would this mage want to be messing with other Supernaturals for fun? What is he or she getting out of this?<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm sure a player could come up with a suitable justification, if they want to. But it's kind of game derailing. It's like if a player of a vampire decided &quot;Actually, I think I'll just hang around in my library and read for the next 200 years.&quot; There's nothing stopping a player from doing that, I suppose, but it wouldn't make for a very fun game. On the other hand, it could make for a fun antagonist in a Vampire game.<br /> <br /> (Also, for the character to set up two separate Camarillas and make them perceive the other as Sabbat, they'd need to construct a really complex, long term ritual. And they're probably going to need a pretty high arete to be able to manage everything at once. It's definitely not, IMO, a starting character level feat.)<br /> <br /> That said, there are ways to deal with this kind of mage. If we assume the targets are old and powerful, or have allies who are old and powerful, that increases the likelihood that they'll observe things that will start making them realize that there's some kind of manipulation going on. Old, powerful vampires tend to be paranoid and manipulative themselves. And even if the mage has a correspondence link with one vampire, that doesn't mean he or she necessarily has a link to every one of the vampire's allies, childer or ghouls. I think it a skilled storyteller could turn it into a fun little interlude in a Vampire chronicle, as a break from the usual challenges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T10:43:38-07:00","id":1123545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123527#post1123527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't easy...but I see your point.<br /> <br /> It isn't easy because your mage has to:<br /> * Know about the Sabbat and the Camarilla, be aware of the existence of vampires that aren't aware of each other (if they are the shenanigan can still be made, but there may be resistences and increases on difficulties involved)<br /> * Have Correspondence links with all the vampires involved (I assume inteligent vampires do not leave a ot of data about themselves, nor like to be stalked to get their hair or pictures)<br /> * Cast a spell with enough successes to target all vampires and alter their perceptions for a long time<br /> <br /> But your point it's easy to understand: It's hard to defend yourself against this kind of shenanigans. Other supernaturals haven't a good defense against this kind of Shenanigans. Countermagick doesn't help much because with a ritual you can always get extra successes to surpass any resistence. Mages fare better because there isn't a clear limit on how much successes you can put into a defense to prevent Correspondence (and powerful mages may create &quot;retaliatory&quot; defenses that detect the attempt and do something to kill the mage that's on the other end), [/FONT]they can detect and cut Correspondence link, and they have reasons to expect this kind of attack<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">.<br /> <br /> The best defense against Correspondence (not involving having Correspondence) it's to not give away your location nor information about you. Mages can't attack what they can't detect.</span><br /> [/FONT]<br /> [/FONT]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well if this is a starting character then Arete 3, Correspondence 3 and Mind 3 are all doable. With Mind 3 and Correspondence 3 you can map something much much larger than a city block (potentially a whole city) and your powerful mental capabilities can sift through all the data you have. Let's say we're a VA who thinks the world is a hologram or video game or simulation or similar. They run a search through the city using Mind 1 to boost their mental capacity (better ways to do it I'm sure, you can have multiple minds at once at level 3 I think?) and Correspondence... 2 I think? Definitely 3 or lower. Then you just filter out all things that are mundane. You're outside the range of Obfuscate, so you're finding every Nosferatu in no time at all. Then you just need to examine the fact that the Nosferatu are split into two or more groups (Nosferatu form family groups, it's worth noting). From here you gradually build up info on every Vampire in the city... why? Well in my games the Traditions like having files on supernaturals, but that's just me. If VAs can have a file on every Vampire in a city they're going to do that, if only so they can help other Mages avoid them. So he's on a payroll to find and file every Vampire in the city, at least at first.<br /> <br /> Next our VA uses their Correspondence 3 to look for good opportunities to extract objects that will give C links. Since they can spend as much time examining a haven before dropping in as they like, they are unlikely to fail... if they had Matter 2 it would be as simple as conjuring one of their minor personal affects (one tool in a set of lockpicks, one tie from a tie rack).<br /> <br /> With the C links for all of the Vampires who are plugged into Elysium sorted out, they prepare a big, big ritual. Risky. The ritual is a brief but vivid hallucination for half of the Vampires detailing a raid by the Sabbat killing the other half. Then repeat with the other half.<br /> <br /> Next ritual is to take the same links and create hallucinations, essentially a potent derangement or unyielding mind control where they register the other half of the Vampires in the city as generic Sabbat thugs.<br /> <br /> NOW I know that this is a HUGE undertaking and very, very risky... so my question isn't &quot;is this realistic&quot;, it's &quot;how can I make this BETTER?&quot; How do we shift the odds more in our favour? Let's assume that this is all happening in Downtimes, that a Session is taking place once a week in-universe, we have 6 downtimes (one per day) and we're gaining 3-4 EXP per session. What's the trajectory? What are we aiming for?<br /> <br /> As for why we're doing it; fun? I mean people kill Vampires for fun canonically (roughly 10% of Hunters are thrillseekers according to Hunters Hunted ll), can't our Mage do this simply for the love of it? As a side note it's a great excuse to increase Arete at the end of it if successful; you've essentially hacked the NPCs (if we're taking a video game analogy) in a city to all go Rage-Mode on eachother, which is pretty nice modding/hacking... and that hints at the mutable underlying nature of the &quot;game&quot;, meaning a quest to increase Arete isn't ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Now, counter-intelligence... if a Vampire sees past the mind control, perhaps thanks to Dementation or Auspex or high Willpower, what do we do with them? For starters, no one will believe them at first, so you have a few days to deal with it. I'm pretty sure Mind can make someone Frenzy pretty badly... would that be level 2 or 4? Simply hit them into Frenzy when they are trying to convince other Vampires, they'll seem unstable at the very least.<br /> <br /> As for fighting the growing suspicion, spread a rumour organically (a small thought in one person's mind) that it's all the work of a powerful Malkavian Elder on the other side who wants them to question their commitment to the fight. Are we going to let some Malk Antitribu trick us? No way!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-01-2017, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T10:53:32-07:00","id":1123550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123536#post1123536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the big question: why would this mage want to be messing with other Supernaturals for fun? What is he or she getting out of this?<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm sure a player could come up with a suitable justification, if they want to. But it's kind of game derailing. It's like if a player of a vampire decided &quot;Actually, I think I'll just hang around in my library and read for the next 200 years.&quot; There's nothing stopping a player from doing that, I suppose, but it wouldn't make for a very fun game. On the other hand, it could make for a fun antagonist in a Vampire game.<br /> <br /> (Also, for the character to set up two separate Camarillas and make them perceive the other as Sabbat, they'd need to construct a really complex, long term ritual. And they're probably going to need a pretty high arete to be able to manage everything at once. It's definitely not, IMO, a starting character level feat.)<br /> <br /> That said, there are ways to deal with this kind of mage. If we assume the targets are old and powerful, or have allies who are old and powerful, that increases the likelihood that they'll observe things that will start making them realize that there's some kind of manipulation going on. Old, powerful vampires tend to be paranoid and manipulative themselves. And even if the mage has a correspondence link with one vampire, that doesn't mean he or she necessarily has a link to every one of the vampire's allies, childer or ghouls. I think it a skilled storyteller could turn it into a fun little interlude in a Vampire chronicle, as a break from the usual challenges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does Arete being only 3 matter? You can reroll as many times as you wish, and the difficulties are going to all be 7 or lower... use of links for Correspondence can push this even lower. Plus we can specialize in spreading this exact kind of mayhem, you can do a lot of Spec-ing at character generation if you're careful.<br /> <br /> If an old, powerful Vampire starts to suspect anything, you can work to isolate them. Oh what do you know, a coterie of Vampires who think he's a Sabbat Elder just got inspired to attack his haven... see where I'm going with this? It would be SUPER difficult but it could be doable.<br /> <br /> Worst case scenario, we botch a ritual or someone sees past it and convinces everyone else... how do they find us? What's the risk? Blood Magic can't trace this kind of thing, and the only power I know of to counter this is Mytherceria 2, which can see the flow of non-undead powers. When a blue Vampire starts shouting about &quot;Magickal Mind Control&quot; we can get everyone to brutally beat and burn him I'm sure, he's an outsider and probably the only Kiasyd in the city after all.<br /> <br /> Beyond that the only problem I can see is a POTENT Elder with serious Auspex finding you effortlessly. If the City has an active Methesulah then you're screwed, unfortunately, as no one will know about them in most cases. The best case scenario would be that you pit then against all of the other Cainites before they destroy you, but that's a best case scenario... hmm... We could preempt this by using Correspondence and Mind to protect against others finding you? Like shielding your Mind and your Pattern from being found by Auspex, which is kind of like using C+M when you search for someone with Elder powers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-01-2017, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T11:09:33-07:00","id":1123558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Arete being only 3 matter? You can reroll as many times as you wish, and the difficulties are going to all be 7 or lower... use of links for Correspondence can push this even lower. Plus we can specialize in spreading this exact kind of mayhem, you can do a lot of Spec-ing at character generation if you're careful.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are limits. You can roll a number of times equal to Arete + Willpower. Thus, you get 13 rolls with Arete 3, Willpower 10. That's the maximum a starting character can do.<br /> <br /> But, with 3 dice, even at diff 4-5 you will likely Botch before you roll all those times, and that means Paradox. In a ritual you gain 1 extra point of Paradox per roll, only if you Botch (otherwise you gain normal Paradox), that may be a lot. You can spend a Willpower point to prevent a Botch, but you can do this only one time (at that point, most mages would leave the ritual while they still have their skins).<br /> <br /> If you have Cult background at 5 you can add 5 successes per roll each time you succed, and if other mages join you can get even more, so it's doable from the start. Keep in mind that for a ritual of this magnitude you can make only one roll each 5 hours of ritual (and your Stamina limmits the amount of hours you can ritual non stop).<br /> <br /> Thus, yep, it's an impresive feat, I'm not certain if it can't be pulled by a starting character but it will be hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If an old, powerful Vampire starts to suspect anything, you can work to isolate them. Oh what do you know, a coterie of Vampires who think he's a Sabbat Elder just got inspired to attack his haven... see where I'm going with this? It would be SUPER difficult but it could be doable. </div> </div> </div>If you're watching them all the time...yes. Conscience roll can likely detect this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Worst case scenario, we botch a ritual or someone sees past it and convinces everyone else... how do they find us? What's the risk? Blood Magic can't trace this kind of thing, and the only power I know of to counter this is Mytherceria 2, which can see the flow of non-undead powers. When a blue Vampire starts shouting about &quot;Magickal Mind Control&quot; we can get everyone to brutally beat and burn him I'm sure, he's an outsider and probably the only Kiasyd in the city after all. </div> </div> </div>And that's the issue, Mage it's unbalanced in crossover. You may want to houserule this a little if you don't want vampires to be sitting ducks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We could preempt this by using Correspondence and Mind to protect against others finding you? Like shielding your Mind and your Pattern from being found by Auspex, which is kind of like using C+M when you search for someone with Elder powers... </div> </div> </div>I think it's *doable*, but Elders tend to enter in the terrain of &quot;he surpasses your defense because I say so&quot;. Protecting your connection it's good vs mages, of course, at that point it's an armamentalist escalation between you and the people that want's to find you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-01-2017, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T11:28:26-07:00","id":1123566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> NOW I know that this is a HUGE undertaking and very, very risky... so my question isn't &quot;is this realistic&quot;, it's &quot;how can I make this BETTER?&quot; How do we shift the odds more in our favour? Let's assume that this is all happening in Downtimes, that a Session is taking place once a week in-universe, we have 6 downtimes (one per day) and we're gaining 3-4 EXP per session. What's the trajectory? What are we aiming for?<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>The REAL problem for vampires it's the distance and understanding what's happening. They have little ways to know you're there (the rare hacker that discovers you're following them in the net, the elder with alies you didn't know, the rare elder that just sees trough your attempt and/or can resist it). Want to make it better?, Find your way into the Umbra, add Spirit 2 and cast from the Umbra, now only vampires with super rare powers can try to stop you (a Tremere with a lvl 5 ritual can get to you, but she has to find you in the Umbra, naked). Probably at that point vampires need to stop being arrogant, and get help from a mage (assuming they know enough about the supernatural world to even think about that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-01-2017, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T12:37:18-07:00","id":1123598,"title":"","content":"I'm still a bit hung up on the &quot;why&quot; of all this. Just from a storytelling perspective. I can imagine a lot of fun chronicle ideas involving mages as vampire hunters. But to me, the idea of having one Mage (with perhaps a cult) in a room somewhere or even in the Umbra, casting wide net spells to make two sects of Camarilla fight each other/mistake each other for the Sabbat...that doesn't strike me as a fun scenario for my players. All the real action takes place off screen with opponents that don't have much of a chance.<br /> <br /> Because I agree, while I think it would be very difficult for a starting Mage to accomplish all of this, it doesn't take that long for them to become incredibly powerful. Especially if they have time, ritual space, a plan and means to prepare. But how do you construct a game around that without the players getting bored at the lack of challenge?<br /> <br /> Honestly, with the set up of a superpowered being manipulating vampires to fight a needless war from afar, it kind of seems like you're using Mage to play a Vampire game. Which is fine if that's what you want to do, but it seems kind of unnecessary.<br /> <br /> To me, the scenario sounds a lot more fun/interesting/challenging as a Vampire game, with the players taking the role of vampire instead. Some vampire elder from another city messages the players' Prince/Bishop/whatever and explains that there's something very weird going on, and the players then have to figure out what exactly is happening. As relatively weak newcomers, they're not likely to attract the Mage's attention right away, and therefore, they neutralize the Mage's biggest edge: preparation and long term rituals for successes. Even if the Mage starts to realize that the player characters are a threat, he's going to have to find a way to anchor his Correspondence sight to them. In the mean time, clever players can make alliances, sabotage his mortal resources, and do a lot of other damage to his long term plans.<br /> <br /> It seems like it'd be more fun to be the underdogs taking down an unbeatable opponent than it would be to be the very powerful mage picking his targets off with no real challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":".  just tweaking for coherence, sorry 08-01-2017, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T13:05:09-07:00","id":1123607,"title":"","content":"Indeed, I agree. But I think thts thought experiment it's more to exemplify &quot;features&quot; of the system that do not traduce well to other systems, than to develop a character.<br /> <br /> Correspondence leaves no defense for vampires. I pointed that Umbra doesn't traduce well to vampire either, because most vampires can't go there.<br /> <br /> Mage gives you better tools to deal with such an hipotetical bothersome manipulator, not because mages are able to &quot;counter&quot; this attack, but because they can get &quot;off the grid&quot; by blocking Corr, use Mind to slip from this control, and find the enemy by following the trail to it's base...all of this would be very hard for a vampire PC to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T13:10:00-07:00","id":1123610,"title":"","content":"That's true.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that I'm surprised there isn't a Thaumaturgical path dealing with the Umbra. The Tremere were Hermetics after all, and they have to have known of its existence. Wouldn't it make sense for at least one of the old Council members to experiment in that direction?<br /> <br /> Or for that matter, given how paranoid they tend to be, I'm rather surprised that there isn't some kind of anti-scrying path. But then, it might be less of a matter that the Tremere wouldn't have such things, and more of a matter of the game never fleshing those out because the likelihood of them coming up in a normal Vampire game is pretty much non-existent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T13:32:26-07:00","id":1123616,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that providing rituals to deal with common mage shenanigans (something for space, something for time, something for spirits, and something dealing with &quot;pure magic&quot;) would be interesting for a crossover universe...at least as Elder stuff.<br /> <br /> Now, Thaumaturgy it's far from common, and it's problematic in itself. For instance, a ritual makes you immaterial, another makes you immune to Presence and Dominate. Combine the two and you are &quot;Brujah proof&quot;, and likely able to tank an entire Eliseum by yourself (barring rare mental/spiritual Disciplines). And we aren't talking of elder levels here, it's not that expensive. It's OP, but I think that's ok to some extent: Magic it's supposed to be scary.<br /> Many of the &quot;problems&quot; perceived in magick are present in blood magick too...in part because it's flexible (not so much, but it is), but also because writers and ST often do not have balance in mind. Here the ST also has to judge what's OK and what's OP as hell and should be baned (or made more difficult).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-01-2017, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T15:10:37-07:00","id":1123653,"title":"","content":"Tremere, being vampires from a mage tradition, probably have some rituals that make them harder to track. I'd rule Obfuscate functions a lot like Arcane when trying to use Correspondence.<br /> <br /> Mages can work the base roots of the tree of reality, so of course they present problems in adjudicating. Yet in over 30 years of gaming, I can not think of an RPG where humans had choices were someone has not had to make a ruling where the rules were silent. In Mage, so much of what your character can do in game is based on what they can imagine and believe, that the Storyteller has to do a lot more work making rulings than in a game where you have few options and clear rules.<br /> <br /> The more open nature of Mage is one reason my early campaigns of Mage weren't very good. I was too literal. Once I got into focusing more on story concerns and characters than being like a judge following RAW (rules as written) precisely, the games were more fun. I'm fine with turning vampires into lawnchairs, but it's not easy to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T15:16:45-07:00","id":1123654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123598#post1123598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still a bit hung up on the &quot;why&quot; of all this. Just from a storytelling perspective. I can imagine a lot of fun chronicle ideas involving mages as vampire hunters. But to me, the idea of having one Mage (with perhaps a cult) in a room somewhere or even in the Umbra, casting wide net spells to make two sects of Camarilla fight each other/mistake each other for the Sabbat...that doesn't strike me as a fun scenario for my players. All the real action takes place off screen with opponents that don't have much of a chance.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because its a silly strawman argument. Its like &quot;what keeps a nexus crawler from attacking you on the toilet?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T16:07:29-07:00","id":1123675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123482#post1123482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He doesn't have time. SOmething with a &quot;Go first Power&quot; kills him while he's in the bathroom. What do you mean my KJ with principle of motion is wasting his time running around killing mages who don't have time? Apparently if I don't do this they will just sit in their room and work on mind and correspondence do mess with us. So premptively kill all mages!<br /> <br /> Replace this with Spirit of the Fray for Werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>How can you reach something that's outside of space?<br /> <br /> Going first doesn't help you if you can't reach the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T16:31:55-07:00","id":1123689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123467#post1123467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See now all I can see is a Correspondence 3, Mind 3 Illusionist who sts in their house and screws with other Supernaturals for fun.<br /> <br /> &quot;See, I managed to get the Vampires in my city to set up two separate Camarilla courts, being unaware of the other. Then I made them perceive eachother as Sabbat and watched the fireworks... what do you mean I'm wasting my talents?!<br /> <br /> <br /> With the C links for all of the Vampires who are plugged into Elysium sorted out, they prepare a big, big ritual. Risky. The ritual is a brief but vivid hallucination for half of the Vampires detailing a raid by the Sabbat killing the other half. Then repeat with the other half.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the most ridiculous post I've ever read.<br /> <br /> You're trying to make the Kindred kill each other. This would involve overcoming 1) The social bonds of Kindred 2) The self-interest of Kindred 3) Personal values of the Kindred 4) Clan social rules 5) Camarilla / Sect structures, rules, incentives, and positions 6) Authority of wiser and/or stronger Kindred 7) The self-preservation instinct.<br /> <br /> This is not a Coincidental Mind 3 Correspondence 3. This is a Vulgar Mind 5 Correspondence 5, with many successes needed. So many that the Ritual is practically a given to not succeed against a group of Kindred; it wouldn't succeed against a single Kindred as well, I'd say.<br /> <br /> And it makes the Mage look like he is playing the Jyhad, at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-01-2017, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T17:03:45-07:00","id":1123705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123689#post1123689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .<br /> And it makes the Mage look like he is playing the Jyhad, at the very least.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mage's connection to each vampire type is their card from the Jyhad or Vampire: The Eternal Struggle CCG. The mage is very likely to be a Marauder with a very powerful Quiet.<br /> <br /> Now for a mage who actually does a little research and finds vampires who dislike each other, the killer nature of many Kindred could override other concerns. My Brujah anarch take out the capitalists despoiling the Earth warrior would not even require magic to kill other vampires. If our Euthanatos group member in the Vampire/Mage game had asked him to kill another vampire, he'd have merely asked what level of collateral damage was acceptable. Of course, my character had as much humanity as the horrible violent brujah terrorist guy in the Brujah splat and was a fanatic, so he'd have be considered an enemy combatant in most societies because his remorse happened only twice in game: once he had to kill a C-suite executive's wife or risk capture due to a failed Stealth roll and so he opted for going full 'black ops.' The other time he had any remorse was when he wounded our Dreamspeakerish party member while under the effects of a Nephandic mind-altering worm that had been put into his blood by the Malkavian in the group and he just started going full autofire with submachine guns and hit his Dreamerspeakerish associate.<br /> <br /> In the end, Mage is a game about Reality on the brink. While games do need rules and chances for success or failure that have systems which allow some odds estimation, Mage is a game of mostly unbounded imagination. Each group should really figure out how hard magic should be to do and what is not fun for the game.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I might have the Marauder using Jhyad or VTES cards show up in my next campaign as a Marauder.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T20:42:11-07:00","id":1123756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123675#post1123675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How can you reach something that's outside of space?<br /> <br /> Going first doesn't help you if you can't reach the target.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Said character wanders around constantly looking for people who just awakened so they never get the chance to level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T01:55:04-07:00","id":1123802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123689#post1123689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the most ridiculous post I've ever read.<br /> <br /> You're trying to make the Kindred kill each other. This would involve overcoming 1) The social bonds of Kindred 2) The self-interest of Kindred 3) Personal values of the Kindred 4) Clan social rules 5) Camarilla / Sect structures, rules, incentives, and positions 6) Authority of wiser and/or stronger Kindred 7) The self-preservation instinct.<br /> <br /> This is not a Coincidental Mind 3 Correspondence 3. This is a Vulgar Mind 5 Correspondence 5, with many successes needed. So many that the Ritual is practically a given to not succeed against a group of Kindred; it wouldn't succeed against a single Kindred as well, I'd say.<br /> <br /> And it makes the Mage look like he is playing the Jyhad, at the very least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind explaining why it's Mind 5 and Correspondence 5? You do realise that the Spheres aren't just &quot;moar powah&quot; as they level up, they widen your abilities in a specific way. Correspondence 3 is all you need for this exercise; it's enough to map out the city, find people, teleport and perform Mind magick from afar. You don't need the power to exist outside of space, or exist in multiple places at once, or overlay multiple places on eachother. You're not doing anything too tricky, like making portals or moving large objects around (for which you'd need Pattern Spheres anyways).<br /> <br /> I can see you needing Mind 4, since that gives far stronger control of people's minds, but hallucinations are achievable below 4, certainly.<br /> <br /> What makes it non-coincidental? It's an illusion. No one is questioning it beyond casting. None of the &quot;witnesses&quot; qualify as witnesses, they're night folk.<br /> <br /> Yes, there is a lot to overcome. It's almost like it's a fun project where you use mental illusions and weak mind control to perform social engineering, and it's almost like Kindred have had huge slaughter-fests against eachother on a semi-regular basis through their history. To be clear, the goal isn't &quot;every Vampire dies&quot;; most of them won't be rushing into the dangerous fights. It's just... well it's just entertaining as something to do in downtimes. Humane vampires aren't going to slaughter others, Elders aren't going to get their hands dirty, this all goes without saying.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In terms of power level, I could see the user needing more Arete than 3, certainly. An Arete of 4 or 5 would be very desirable since it would allow rolls to be extended further and reduce the risk of Botching; plus it also means you can get more successes within the amount of rolls you can perform. Some Avatar and Prime would be good for Quintessence, plus with Correspondence and Prime you could create a very good tech-based security system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-02-2017, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T07:05:14-07:00","id":1123862,"title":"","content":"Indeed, it depends on how you make it. If the vampires truly didn't know each other (something hard to believe, but let's roll with it), you could use Mind 3 (enough to cause Illusions, enough to cause compulsions and alter emotion as if they were clay, enough for the feared Social Conditioning) to create the idea that Sabbat vampires are on the city, and then to provide both &quot;evidence&quot; and strong feeling/belief that the other vampires are doing Sabbatical stuff. All of this is Coincident as long as you can mantain the illusion, but that would require amounts of lore and luck, and probably a few different rituals with a really high number of successes (I would say on the 20, 'cause it's a bit &quot;goodlike&quot;, + number of vampires + Corr table, but that's an ST call).<br /> <br /> Mind 4 would be needed only if you want to sidestep all clever &quot;framing and paranoia&quot; and just force vampires to go after each other regardless of what they believe or feel, which will have a ludicrously high difficluty and be Vulgar, but actually may require less sucesses, dependant on how hard you think it is to force someone to fight against his will with Mind 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-02-2017, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T08:13:19-07:00","id":1123879,"title":"","content":"I would like to go to a related topic that has to do with previous posts:<br /> <br /> What about area of effect stuff? Area of effect it's a fuzzy area on the rules. It sidesteps the need of extra successes per person affected, making it ideal to influence crowds, but the spell affects everyone, even you (if you are in the area). It's a hammer, not a scalpel.<br /> <br /> The ST can make the spell as difficult as needed, but Mage does offer a few guidelines, like that affecting a city with a sleeping spell would be a minimum of 30 successes (in Revised) and in M20 it's sugested that 5 it's the minimum successes needed to affect an area to begin with. Also, Sphere level seems to limit the Area (at least Forces works that way), but it isn't specified *how*, except in Forces (thus, it's mostly an ST call).<br /> <br /> Nedless to say, this can save you a lot of successes and compensates for new people entering the area (they may be affected too, if the spell it's in effect). This is what you need to do if you want to &quot;Obfuscate&quot; with Mind, or do a &quot;Majesty&quot; stunt.<br /> <br /> But there's an aspect of &quot;area&quot; that it's even less explored than the amount of successes needed, and that's when magick runs trough a medium. For instance, a magical song it's said to affect everyone that hears it, but not those that can't hear it. This generates an area that's quite variable dependan't on external factors (not only walls *may* block your magic, deaf people would be immune while people with enhanced senses may be affected from far away).<br /> <br /> But what if we add a digital medium?, Will your magical song affect all people watching your live performance? . Of course, this depends on Paradigm, but my intent isn't to go there, the raison d'etre for this example it's to make a comparison, because this is something vampires CAN do.<br /> <br /> With Technomancy vampires can affect with their Disciplines A LOT of people (a potentially limitless amount).<br /> <br /> This it's very broken, isn't it? I've heard in other thread to argue that vampires could initiate a pague capable of destroying the world by using this method, unless the Camarilla quickly contains the problem somehow:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Vampires went &quot;viral&quot; then judicious use of Dominate and Presence via Technothaum (people who call for help on their phone get a Dominate command to come out into the street and surrender for example) could have newly embraced Vampires embracing before you know it, as just one example. The problem is that if you try and embrace EVERYONE you're left with no blood supply. Any smart Vampire would try and curb this virality.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER I think a group of Vampires trying to get virality could be an interesting Masquerade breach.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...returning to magic(k). What happens when you want to alter the local Consensus in a city or turn everyone in a violent zomby, or anything of the like by abusing Area of Effect? It's controling every one of your You-Tube viewers even possible?. I would say that you <i>can</i>, but you will have to live with the consequences, which usualy means Technocracy kicking yor ass (And, of course, there's the permanent treath of Paradox).<br /> <br /> In Mage we have the Technocracy to clean up if a mage want's to do anything nasty in a grand scale, and they're scarily good at doing it. Think about the kind of resources they have: Technocracy has people 24/7 reading the future with Time 2 to detect any &quot;world changing&quot; events, they have big radars that detect outputs of magic (but they only have the resources to focus on really big displays of power), conbining both they could detect great works of magick before they happen...and they can travel really quick with Correspondence, deploying any amount of force (including supernatural mind control) basically anywhere.<br /> <br /> Actually, I would say that Mage (thanks to paradox and the efficiency of the Technocracy) has it's ass better covered in regards of big spells running trough the net/media than Vampire. Wouldn't you think so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-02-2017, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T08:30:57-07:00","id":1123884,"title":"","content":"But what if the Technocracy does it?...well, in Mage the market colapse was caused by Syndicate members that botched and released a big Paradox backlash doing this kind of mojo...Technocracy has laws forbbiding this kind of shenanigans because of that. But if they tried...I guess it would be an interesting plot point for the Traditions to try to stop them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T14:20:36-07:00","id":1124005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123884#post1123884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what if the Technocracy does it?...well, in Mage the market colapse was caused by Syndicate members that botched and released a big Paradox backlash doing this kind of mojo...Technocracy has laws forbbiding this kind of shenanigans because of that. But if they tried...I guess it would be an interesting plot point for the Traditions to try to stop them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't the crash caused by Anarchs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T09:30:37-07:00","id":1124336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't the crash caused by Anarchs?</div> </div> </div> </div>So say the Anarchs. Syndicate (in their revised book) stated that it was their fault. A few members made a financial experiment trying to end scarcity, it didn't work, now they were declared roge. This it's one of the complaints NWO holds against the Syndicate in the verge of the &quot;technocratic civil war&quot;<br /> <br /> This is one of THESE cases in crossover...were things don't add up. Thus, it's up to the ST.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Anarchs hadn't anything to do with the crach, but they took the credit because a few Ventrue were negatively affected, and being responsable made them look B@DA$$ (you can't fuck with us!, we have powers beyond your elderly understanding!). I seem to remember Anarchs were very proud and uppity with this &quot;feat&quot;.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Anarchs caused the crash and the Syndicate decided to took the blame. This may seem weird because <i>this doesn't make them look good</i> (It caused no end of problems with the Technocratic budget, while reducing the faith in modern economy and banks, causing everyone to hate the Syndicate), however they were in the verge of a war with the NWO (and they knew it). Admiting that a bunch of low level vampires managed to get under their system, and caused them soo much trouble, would be even worse for the image of strenght that they want to project than taking the blame &lt;<i>Oh, those Syndicate beancounters allowed a bunch of techno-renegades to trash economy, this is what hapens when you trust something to a &quot;technocrat&quot; that knows nothing about tech! , maybe our ItX/Feed hackers should take control of economy to prevent this from happening&gt;</i><br /> <br /> Of course, books do not point to any of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T09:55:42-07:00","id":1124341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1124336#post1124336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So say the Anarchs. Syndicate (in their revised book) stated that it was their fault. A few members made a financial experiment trying to end scarcity, it didn't work, now they were declared roge. This it's one of the complaints NWO holds against the Syndicate in the verge of the &quot;technocratic civil war&quot;<br /> <br /> This is one of THESE cases in crossover...were things don't add up. Thus, it's up to the ST.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Anarchs hadn't anything to do with the crach, but they took the credit because a few Ventrue were negatively affected, and being responsable made them look B@DA$$ (you can't fuck with us!, we have powers beyond your elderly understanding!). I seem to remember Anarchs were very proud and uppity with this &quot;feat&quot;.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Anarchs caused the crash and the Syndicate decided to took the blame. This may seem weird because <i>this doesn't make them look good</i> (It caused no end of problems with the Technocratic budget, while reducing the faith in modern economy and banks, causing everyone to hate the Syndicate), however they were in the verge of a war with the NWO (and they knew it). Admiting that a bunch of low level vampires managed to get under their system, and caused them soo much trouble, would be even worse for the image of strenght that they want to project than taking the blame &lt;<i>Oh, those Syndicate beancounters allowed a bunch of techno-renegades to trash economy, this is what hapens when you trust something to a &quot;technocrat&quot; that knows nothing about tech! , maybe our ItX/Feed hackers should take control of economy to prevent this from happening&gt;</i><br /> <br /> Of course, books do not point to any of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could even be that both are right, at least partially. The Anarchs had some plans in motion to strike against Ventrue business interests. Right as it was going off, though, some Syndicate members botched their rolls, generating Paradox that exasperated the damage being caused by the Anarchs. The two events going off at the same time made the resulting market downturn worse than if either had gone off alone. And of course both groups would only see their side of the events, resulting in bragging rights for the Anarchs and an embarrassment for the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> Edit: Now personally, I'm more inclined to believe that the Syndicate caused the crash by mistake, and the Anarchs took credit for it, than I am to believe the Anarchs caused it on purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 08-03-2017, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:57:27-07:00","id":1124419,"title":"","content":"I think the likeliest thing in a unified WoD would be that the Anarchs did as described in Anarchs Unbound and Dominated, Presenced and blood bound high-ranking financial workers to influence their decisions and make them work in a more risky way. Following this they used Technothaum to make the market more volatile until... boom.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile this was exacerbated by the Syndicate seeking to eradicate the problems of the market; they were working in quicksand thanks to the Anarchs when they had all reason to expect a beach. The two, together, is what made the crash so spectacular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T12:43:33-07:00","id":1124436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1124341#post1124341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Now personally, I'm more inclined to believe that the Syndicate caused the crash by mistake, and the Anarchs took credit for it, than I am to believe the Anarchs caused it on purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>By Anarchs did you mean &quot;Chaotic Good Vampires who would NEVER do something bad&quot;? Anarchs may be the nicest Sect on average, but they're still blood-drinking monsters who have rejected the social contract, like almost all Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T12:49:57-07:00","id":1124443,"title":"","content":"Well I can see the Anarchs wanting to do it, but I have a problem when mages are ludicrously ignorant about things that should be obvious.<br /> <br /> If the Syndicate had such a breach, they have to start searching someone to cut it's head off. Even if they would take the blame, they WILL want heads to roll...and mages have all the resources to detect something as stupidly evident as mentally manipulating people on power to take dumb desitions.<br /> With Entropy 2/Data 2 they can detect why/where the system crashed (and have a good idea of who make the bad choices, but really, you can do this without magic), then with Time 2 + PU 1-2 + Mind 2 they should be able to detect &quot;deviant manipulation&quot; even after it was removed, and discover that these vives are vampirical would be a matter of searching the databases. After that, you know what happened, albeit you probably don't know *who*. All of this it's fairly standard research.<br /> <br /> Thus, I cannot believe the Syndicate is ignorant about what happened, unless the Anarchs had a very small part on the disaster. I can believe they know but preffer to hide the info, though, much like Project Invictus hides the corruption of the SPD, while they deal with the problem (and with the culprits, there's no such thing as privacy when you have someone with precognition + Spheres on your trail, being at the other side of the net won't protect your identity from precognition+ far sight + Forces 1 to read all the flow of data, add a PU specialist 'cus we're searching for deviant influence).<br /> <br /> Really, if your mage did something that blatant in a game (using Mind + Correspondence) you would have the Syndicate on your door before you can say &quot;oh s***t&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-03-2017, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T14:40:08-07:00","id":1124482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1124436#post1124436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By Anarchs did you mean &quot;Chaotic Good Vampires who would NEVER do something bad&quot;? Anarchs may be the nicest Sect on average, but they're still blood-drinking monsters who have rejected the social contract, like almost all Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't think the Anarchs would be too moral to do it. I'm saying I don't think they COULD pull it off on their own. Their bark is worse than their bite (figuratively, of course). Engineering a market collapse is not easy, and keeping it a secret from the very Clan they are targeting even more so. At the very least, I believe more in the Syndicate screwing it up bad <i>by mistake</i> than I do the Anarchs pulling it off <i>on purpose</i>. All the plans of mice, men, and vampires pale in comparison to good ol' fashioned incompetence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T12:11:47-07:00","id":1125299,"title":"","content":"He, who knows...it could even have been the fault of humans, like in real life. The problem for the Syndicate it's that they were left in charge of &quot;controling economy&quot;-this was &quot;their fault&quot; regardless of who actually caused the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T00:48:58-07:00","id":1126614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123802#post1123802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind explaining why it's Mind 5 and Correspondence 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need Mind 5 because Mind 5 is \u201cControl Subconscious\u201d. Mind 3 - \u201cProject Illusions\u201d is not enough to do what you described. You need Mind 5 to overcome, among other things:<br /> 1) The social bonds of Kindred 2) The self-interest of Kindred 3) Personal values of the Kindred 4) Clan social rules 5) Camarilla / Sect structures, rules, incentives, and positions 6) Authority of wiser and/or stronger Kindred 7) The self-preservation instinct.<br /> <br /> Because you need Mind 5, you also need Correspondence 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1123802#post1123802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's almost like it's a fun project where you use mental illusions and weak mind control to perform social engineering (\u2026) It's just... well it's just entertaining as something to do in downtimes. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call it \u201cfun\u201d or \u201centertaining\u201d. These are the Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-09-2017, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T01:33:40-07:00","id":1126619,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3254_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3254\" data-vbnamecard=\"3254\">Muad'Dib</a> Well having read How do you DO That, I've discovered that mental coercion of supernaturals is Willpower + 3, and those with Dominate or similar is Willpower + 5. If you're controlling a group then it's based on the highest difficulty present... the section ends by saying &quot;Vampires are not your bitches&quot;, so I can see that the developers of M20 had stuff like this in mind.<br /> <br /> With that said I still believe that mental illusions would do the trick. Your social bonds don't mean squat if your friend LOOKS and SOUNDS like a member of the Sabbat, and same in reverse. Plus illusions aren't direct coercion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T02:49:44-07:00","id":1126634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1126619#post1126619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that said I still believe that mental illusions would do the trick. Your social bonds don't mean squat if your friend LOOKS and SOUNDS like a member of the Sabbat, and same in reverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by the part &quot;sounds like a member of the Sabbat&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T02:54:03-07:00","id":1126635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1126634#post1126634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by the part &quot;sounds like a member of the Sabbat&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well edit out whatever they're actually saying, add in some stuff based on the people's preconceptions of the Sabbat to make it stronger. Draw inspiration from their own beliefs and expectations; in fact you could make the Ritual work so that their collective stereotypes of the Sabbat are what forms the illusion itself.<br /> <br /> If they expect a martyr yelling about proving himself to the Dark Father, they get that, if they expect a Tzimisce Neonate yelling about how he'll wear their flesh, they get that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T03:02:46-07:00","id":1126638,"title":"","content":"And what do you mean by the part &quot;looks like a member of the Sabbat&quot;?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T03:34:34-07:00","id":1126641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1126638#post1126638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what do you mean by the part &quot;looks like a member of the Sabbat&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you can mash up their own preconceptions and excerpts from their memories, but...<br /> <br /> - Pack Tattoos<br /> - Body modifications<br /> - Punk aesthetic<br /> - Generally inhuman demeanor<br /> - Pseudo-religious Sabbat symbols<br /> - Trophies; Werewolf fangs as talismans as an example","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T00:36:33-07:00","id":1127003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1126619#post1126619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that said I still believe that mental illusions would do the trick. Your social bonds don't mean squat if your friend LOOKS and SOUNDS like a member of the Sabbat, and same in reverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>So would the Kindred affected by this &quot;mental illusion&quot; that you described think that the other Kindred are still their friend(s), but the friend(s) have joined the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> What do you mean by &quot;and same in reverse&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T01:26:21-07:00","id":1127007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127003#post1127003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would the Kindred affected by this &quot;mental illusion&quot; that you described think that the other Kindred are still their friend(s), but the friend(s) have joined the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> What do you mean by &quot;and same in reverse&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>So the mental illusion is entirely sensory, not conceptual. They don't see their friend. They see a member of the Sabbat. Same goes for their other senses. And the same goes for their friend's perceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T01:53:26-07:00","id":1127012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127007#post1127007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the mental illusion is entirely sensory, not conceptual. They don't see their friend. They see a member of the Sabbat. Same goes for their other senses. And the same goes for their friend's perceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say this would count as Vulgar, instead of Coincidental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T06:19:10-07:00","id":1127084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127012#post1127012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say this would count as Vulgar, instead of Coincidental.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> All of the ruse depends on the vampires not realizing that their perceptions have been changed (because you aren't controlling their actions). I would say it's Coincident if no one notices shit. Remember that Mage runs on HAP, people watching them would believe they're crazy, not that their perceptions have been altered by magic. Most of Mind it's Coincident because of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T06:56:28-07:00","id":1127094,"title":"","content":"Vulgar or not doesn't really matter for difficulty since illusions are still Mind effects that are influencing the vampire' s perceptions. They are still cast against Willpower +3 or +5. It's not any easier that control.<br /> <br /> That said how does this Mage know so much about Vampire politics to be able to do this. Even with a 5 in Lore and with a specialty in Vampires it is highly doubtful you would know enough about the Camerilla and Sabbat to fool the other on a deep level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:30:04-07:00","id":1127102,"title":"","content":"Well, I seem to remember that if you're aware you get to &quot;dodge&quot; with Willpower, and it's another +3 to diff (on top of the &quot;vampire penalty&quot;) because you're being forced to do things against your will.<br /> <br /> Lore wise, with 5 you know more than what most of your subjects know about themselves (your Lore it's equivalent to that of an Elder), with 6 you know how to undo the Curse of Caine (as per Vampire ST book). I would say that 5 it's enough. But, of course, you need to *get* that amount of Lore. It's by no means common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-10-2017, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:33:29-07:00","id":1127105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127102#post1127102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) with 6 you know how to undo the Curse of Caine (as per Vampire ST book) (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Which Storyteller VtM book are you referring to? Can you give the exact page number, as well?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:46:34-07:00","id":1127113,"title":"","content":"I owe you the page umber, but there's a famous Rote in Revised Vampire ST handbook that undoes the Curse (It's Prime 6 + a bunch of high level Spheres). I think it mentioned you needed a lot of Lore or Occult to understand what you're doing, Lore 6 or Occult 7.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would require a little more of Lore because, otherwise, what secrets are saved for Lore 7+?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:00:21-07:00","id":1127119,"title":"","content":"Which Storyteller VtM book were you referring to in regards to the Curse of Cain? Can you give the exact page number?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:18:52-07:00","id":1127135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127119#post1127119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Storyteller VtM book were you referring to in regards to the Curse of Cain? Can you give the exact page number?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, pleases do. If that exists somewhere in print I need to bring that to a friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:29:45-07:00","id":1127140,"title":"","content":"Ok: It's Vampire <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2308/Vampire-Storytellers-Handbook--Revised-Edition?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Storiteller's Handbook Revised</a>. Chapter 6, page 165 (spanish version, in english it should be arrond the same page), Restore Mortality sidebar. And I was wrong, it's <b>Occult 6</b> what you need to know how to undo the curse. In Mage, Occult would act like the poor man's version of Vampire Lore in regards to this specific subject, BUT , I think that the spirit of the rule was to put that knowledge out of reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:46:00-07:00","id":1127148,"title":"","content":"Personally, I prefer <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/242/The-Red-Sign?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Red Sign</a> approach on that subject.<br /> <br /> Red Sign it's a crossover adventure that it's centered arround vampires joining with mages to undo the Curse by using a special ritual casted with the help of an artifact.<br /> <br /> Requiring a special unique item it's silly to me (mages should be able to replicate any effect), but it's insinuated that, perhaps, the artifact just lowers the requisites to &quot;<i>below ArchSpheres</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> The &quot;lore prerequisite&quot; it's covered by having Elder Thaumaturges researching with you, instead of just dots that can be gathered with Past Lives, Totem and whatnot.<br /> <br /> The spell consequences and rules are fuzzy, and may or may not bring the end of times (adequatelly epic).<br /> <br /> It's a whole story...Archmage-level shenanigans should always be stories, regardless of the rules implied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:09:29-07:00","id":1127157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127140#post1127140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (...) BUT , I think that the spirit of the rule was to put that knowledge out of reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:17:49-07:00","id":1127162,"title":"","content":"'cause humans can't have a Trait at 6 (most of the time). And it's implied in the text that few have that kind of knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:22:08-07:00","id":1127165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127162#post1127162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'cause humans can't have a Trait at 6 (most of the time).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this given as a specific rule in any book? I'm sure that Physical Attributes are noted as being out of reach, but are the other ones - like Mental Attributes, or Skills - as well noted as not being achievable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:14:13-07:00","id":1127211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127007#post1127007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the mental illusion is entirely sensory, not conceptual. They don't see their friend. They see a member of the Sabbat. Same goes for their other senses. And the same goes for their friend's perceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're forcing an illusion upon all the senses of Steve the Ventrue that a sort-of-friend, Josh the Brujah, has a werewolf fang necklace and tons of body mods and tattoos and is screaming about how the Camarilla will fall. Steve has worked with Josh off-and-on for maybe 70 years in this city, during which time both have been ally and foe at various times. And you're presuming that this hallucination is enough for Steve to kill Josh? I really don't see how years upon years of experience with someone can be overridden that simply. Mind 3 does not grant enough control to keep Steve from saying, &quot;What the hell, this makes no sense.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you really want to cause vampire civil war with Mind and Correspondence from the comfort of your own home, I think you have a few options:<br /> <br /> First - Mind 3/Correspondence 3 to throw sufficient traumatic thoughts at a vampire to get him to frenzy. Having lots of successes would make the frenzy check harder, and it makes more sense to save up one big hallucination rather than little ones - because he'll start to distrust his senses after it happens the first time. One vampire in frenzy isn't enough, though, and you'd probably need to frenzy most vampires in town - otherwise the remainder will band together and as an organized force, they can take out the others individually. So while it's not a bad way to take out a couple isolated vampires, it doesn't quite create your complete civil war. (You might be able to do this with Mind 2/Correspondence 2 by simply sending the emotion of rage, depending on your ST.)<br /> <br /> Second - Mind 4/Correspondence 4 to forcibly control the conscious mind of many vampires and force them to take a bunch of destructive actions. Again here, depending on what you make them do, they'll probably get a roll or two to break the control, but you could do it on vastly fewer Kindred and turn them into your remote-control special ops squad. You'd need to know how to use a spec ops squad to take down lots of vampires quickly, so lots of research, but in theory plausible.<br /> <br /> Third and most reliable - Mind 5/Correspondence 5 to slowly convert individual vampires into Manchurian candidates by rewriting their subconscious with specific triggers and new personalities embedded underneath. Nobody realizes anything is up until they all activate. You no longer need to directly control them - which would be a stress on the mage's own mind - because you've written new personalities specific to the tasks you've set them. You don't even need to know that much about HOW they should go about their destruction, because you're giving them a genuine motivation and letting them figure it out to the best of their abilities.<br /> <br /> So it's not that you CAN'T do what you want with lower-level spheres - it's that your results are cruder and less effective, and require more planning/successes than they otherwise might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:20:03-07:00","id":1127213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127094#post1127094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vulgar or not doesn't really matter for difficulty since illusions are still Mind effects that are influencing the vampire' s perceptions. They are still cast against Willpower +3 or +5. It's not any easier that control.<br /> <br /> That said how does this Mage know so much about Vampire politics to be able to do this. Even with a 5 in Lore and with a specialty in Vampires it is highly doubtful you would know enough about the Camerilla and Sabbat to fool the other on a deep level.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difficulty of CONTROLLING a Vampire is +3 or +5. Whammying them with &quot;Kill Eachother&quot; is very very difficult. Vampires have no innate resistance to mental illusions, other than potent Auspex, and the innate Wits + Occult roll that Vampires *may* get to resist Magick depending on your ST (and if you have 0 occult it's no roll at all; can't attempt a Knowledge roll with 0 in the Knowledge, and this reflects your average non-Tremere I'd argue).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:20:36-07:00","id":1127214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127211#post1127211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) If you really want to cause vampire civil war with Mind and Correspondence from the comfort of your own home, I think you have a few options: (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you using the term &quot;comfort of your own home&quot; in regards to a True Mage casting Effects on the Kindred?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:24:55-07:00","id":1127216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127211#post1127211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're forcing an illusion upon all the senses of Steve the Ventrue that a sort-of-friend, Josh the Brujah, has a werewolf fang necklace and tons of body mods and tattoos and is screaming about how the Camarilla will fall. Steve has worked with Josh off-and-on for maybe 70 years in this city, during which time both have been ally and foe at various times. And you're presuming that this hallucination is enough for Steve to kill Josh? I really don't see how years upon years of experience with someone can be overridden that simply. Mind 3 does not grant enough control to keep Steve from saying, &quot;What the hell, this makes no sense.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't hard to grasp! I really can't believe it's taken this long...<br /> <br /> He doesn't see Josh. He sees a Member of the Sabbat. He doesn't see &quot;Josh as a Member of the Sabbat&quot;, I never said this or even implied this. There's no reason to keep anything &quot;real&quot; in the illusion beyond location and rough size.<br /> <br /> There is no reason to disbelieve the illusion in this case; it's just a random Sabbat thug, a face drawn randomly from the concepts of &quot;Generic Sabbat Thug&quot; in the collective minds of the Vampires present, and the clothing and accessories I outlined.<br /> <br /> Vampires 1-3 have an illusion of Vampires 4-6 as Generic Sabbat. Vampires 4-6 have an illusion of Vampires 1-3 as Generic Sabbat. Does this demand a big ritual with many successes, and a lot of preparation? Yes. It's a project for a kind of dickish person with a twisted sense of humour, who is willing to invest a lot of time and Quintessence and take some mild risks. I did outline how they would find Correspondence links for the Vampires in question, and how they'd find them in the first place. Anyways with this method, and some luck, they could take out Coteries one at a time. Getting the Camarilla of a city to kill itself (or most of itself, there are those who will prove immune thanks to Elder Auspex, exceptional Wits + Occult, Wards and counter-magic) would be pretty impressive, and having recordings of it (our Mage is a VA, CCTV footage and recordings via smart devices that happen to be present) would make for a nice way to show off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-10-2017, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:28:11-07:00","id":1127217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127094#post1127094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said how does this Mage know so much about Vampire politics to be able to do this. Even with a 5 in Lore and with a specialty in Vampires it is highly doubtful you would know enough about the Camerilla and Sabbat to fool the other on a deep level.</div> </div> </div> </div>And with Correspondence and Mind at 3, how is it difficult by any measure to simply collect this information? Vampires do *talk* about these things around eachother; hell, if you observe a Fledgeling you can learn EVERYTHING you need to know from their Sire educating them.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of Mage = Win in any setting, even MtA (a Mage in VtM couldn't do much of the stuff I'm suggesting, they're stuck with Auspex, Dominate etc.), but there aren't many serious obstacles for a Mage learning Vampiric Lore if they have Correspondence and Mind. They really can just collect information over time. And once ONE Virtual Adept has this information there's a bloody (heh) PDF on the subject available to download at a Chantry near you...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:54:40-07:00","id":1127226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127216#post1127216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't hard to grasp! I really can't believe it's taken this long...<br /> <br /> He doesn't see Josh. He sees a Member of the Sabbat. He doesn't see &quot;Josh as a Member of the Sabbat&quot;, I never said this or even implied this. There's no reason to keep anything &quot;real&quot; in the illusion beyond location and rough size.<br /> <br /> There is no reason to disbelieve the illusion in this case; it's just a random Sabbat thug, a face drawn randomly from the concepts of &quot;Generic Sabbat Thug&quot; in the collective minds of the Vampires present, and the clothing and accessories I outlined.<br /> <br /> Vampires 1-3 have an illusion of Vampires 4-6 as Generic Sabbat. Vampires 4-6 have an illusion of Vampires 1-3 as Generic Sabbat. Does this demand a big ritual with many successes, and a lot of preparation? Yes. It's a project for a kind of dickish person with a twisted sense of humour, who is willing to invest a lot of time and Quintessence and take some mild risks. I did outline how they would find Correspondence links for the Vampires in question, and how they'd find them in the first place. Anyways with this method, and some luck, they could take out Coteries one at a time. Getting the Camarilla of a city to kill itself (or most of itself, there are those who will prove immune thanks to Elder Auspex, exceptional Wits + Occult, Wards and counter-magic) would be pretty impressive, and having recordings of it (our Mage is a VA, CCTV footage and recordings via smart devices that happen to be present) would make for a nice way to show off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. That's a more interesting effect.<br /> <br /> For that to work, the illusion has to be in place before Steve encounters Josh. If Josh suddenly transforms before his eyes he won't believe it. So you sort of need a time-delayed hallucination - when Steve next encounters a Kindred, his senses of that Kindred are overwritten with that of Generic Sabbat Dude.<br /> <br /> I'll agree Mind 3 is sufficient for that, but you also need some sort of Time as well, and maybe Entropy. The hallucination can't start until he encounters a Kindred, but it has to start at that exact moment so he doesn't disbelieve it. M20 says hanging a spell requires Time 4, which I think is kind of silly - I'd houserule it down to Time 3. Then add Entropy 1, or Matter 1/Life 1 to detect when a Kindred is entering his field of view.<br /> <br /> That's actually not unlike my Manchurian candidate idea. You'd cast these spells all day long and when night falls, lots of vampires will have these hanging over their head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:59:57-07:00","id":1127231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127226#post1127226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotcha. That's a more interesting effect.<br /> <br /> For that to work, the illusion has to be in place before Steve encounters Josh. If Josh suddenly transforms before his eyes he won't believe it. So you sort of need a time-delayed hallucination - when Steve next encounters a Kindred, his senses of that Kindred are overwritten with that of Generic Sabbat Dude.<br /> <br /> I'll agree Mind 3 is sufficient for that, but you also need some sort of Time as well, and maybe Entropy. The hallucination can't start until he encounters a Kindred, but it has to start at that exact moment so he doesn't disbelieve it. M20 says hanging a spell requires Time 4, which I think is kind of silly - I'd houserule it down to Time 3. Then add Entropy 1, or Matter 1/Life 1 to detect when a Kindred is entering his field of view.<br /> <br /> That's actually not unlike my Manchurian candidate idea. You'd cast these spells all day long and when night falls, lots of vampires will have these hanging over their head.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a very good point! However, you could do it manually.<br /> <br /> Simply observe via Correspondence once the ritual is completed, waiting to put the finishing touch and fire it off. When one or more Vampires is JUST about to run into one or more other Vampires, fire off the ritual. You can construct the clean-cut appearance too; a mental illusion of a flash of blinding light, gunfire, disorienting acrid smoke, and when it fades we have our Sabbat Illusions in place.<br /> <br /> But yes, I see that making the ritual conditional would probably make it much stronger. Simply work together with another VA in your story I suppose? Not going to learn Time (which I find a tad niche myself) just to pull this off ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T12:00:20-07:00","id":1127232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127217#post1127217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) (a Mage in VtM couldn't do much of the stuff I'm suggesting, they're stuck with Auspex, Dominate etc.) (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this actually written in most V:tM books? Can you name the books you know that this is suggested - that True Mages should use Auspex, Dominate, Thaumaturgy etc. in V:tM to simulate their True Magick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T12:41:44-07:00","id":1127246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127232#post1127232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you name the books you know that this is suggested - that True Mages should use Auspex, Dominate, Thaumaturgy etc. in V:tM to simulate their True Magick?</div> </div> </div> </div>V:TM Revised - Page 278<br /> V:20th - Page 381","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T12:47:20-07:00","id":1127250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually a very good point! However, you could do it manually.<br /> <br /> Simply observe via Correspondence once the ritual is completed, waiting to put the finishing touch and fire it off. When one or more Vampires is JUST about to run into one or more other Vampires, fire off the ritual. You can construct the clean-cut appearance too; a mental illusion of a flash of blinding light, gunfire, disorienting acrid smoke, and when it fades we have our Sabbat Illusions in place.<br /> <br /> But yes, I see that making the ritual conditional would probably make it much stronger. Simply work together with another VA in your story I suppose? Not going to learn Time (which I find a tad niche myself) just to pull this off ;-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's an example step by step of how I think this could be achieved, I'm going to use Science, but it doesn't need to be the only option. It uses Mind 3 / Data 3. Lots of brain hacking (I imagine resistances could be felt as mental firewalls and such <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), I don't think other Spheres would be <i>necessary </i>but Prime and/or Time could help, and it would be great to have ritual helpers:<br /> <br /> 1. You need to discover a very crucial info on vampiric business in the city: Who they are.<br /> <br /> You can do this, for instance, by discovering a careless vampire and hacking her mind trough a street camera, reading her toughts to discover who knows the local faces of the Cam, if the vampire doesn't know that, you can discover who will know. Unless most of the Elyseum never hunt outside their havens this should be easy because of &quot;the social bonds between vampires&quot;. Everyone has an idea about who is who.<br /> <br /> 2. You have to set an unparaleled Correspondence spy net that would be the envy of any NWO agent. You may have to set the Correspondence/Data connections individually, a complex task made possible thanks to your prior research that may take days or weeks, a few Elders that do not leave home or manage to avoid all cameras and other &quot;instruments&quot; of yours may present complications. if you manage this you could put the local Cam to it's knees because...<br /> <br /> 3. You can cast spells and read minds with impunity. You not only know who the Sabbat are, but, more importantly, you know what the local vampires think about the Sabbat (which may not be accurate, but you're playing to their expectations).<br /> <br /> (These points are key. If vampires can detect something it's going on, and detect where you are/what are you doing, they could potentially stop you. A Partial success with these shenanigans may be enough to start a ruckus, but would leave loose threads)<br /> <br /> 4.Increase natural vampiric paranoia about a Sabbat infiltration in the city. Really, nothing should be easier, vampires live in constant paranoia.<br /> <br /> You could plant the idea that the sect it's present by fiddling with the memory of past hunts (construct a &quot;encounter with the Sabbat&quot; in a night where the vamp failed to feed. It doesn't need to be very realistic, it needs to live up to Cam expectations to startle the local vampires). You could even plant the suspicion that some fringe members of the Cam may have switched sides, just to make everyone a bit more paranoid<br /> <br /> 5. At this point the fun has already started. Vampires and paranoia are like gunpowder and fire. Blood it's going to be spilled (perhaps even yours)<br /> <br /> If they realize something odd it's happening, they may suspect someone it's Dominating people (fiddling with memory), but vampiric suspicion starts at home, not at some other splat.<br /> <br /> Also, since you have their minds on speed dial (or, as an alternative, you could have their toughts being projected non-stop to your computers while keeping a map with their location-this would be very potent mojo!) you can make those toughts loose importance, a la Technocratic social conditioning.<br /> <br /> More than likely, they will search Sabbat infiltrators, either because they fell for it, or just to be sure. And, sure enough, they're going to find &quot;the Sabbat&quot;, because you're going to make it happen. To engineer an encounter should be easy enough for someone that posseses this massive net (just take advantage that vampires are searching for Sabbat, induce a few vampires to go to some place without knowing that another group it's alread there).<br /> <br /> 5. You project the illusion when you know vampires are about to meet using your gigantic net, overriding all five senses- you can do this as suggested by 11twiggins, after all, you know more or less where and when vampires are going to encounter, but Time 4 would make things much easier, allowing you to sleep and have sweet dreams while vampires kill each other)- Congrats, you've &quot;found the sabbat&quot;, too bad that it wasn't the actual Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-10-2017, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T12:54:49-07:00","id":1127256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127232#post1127232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this actually written in most V:tM books? Can you name the books you know that this is suggested - that True Mages should use Auspex, Dominate, Thaumaturgy etc. in V:tM to simulate their True Magick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Index of V20, look at the Mages there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T12:56:31-07:00","id":1127257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127250#post1127250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) (allowing you to sleep and have sweet dreams while vampires kill each other) (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you explain why a True Mage (or a group of True Mages) would have sweet dreams - or would want to have sweet dreams - after casting what you described on a Kindred (or a group of Kindred) ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:00:59-07:00","id":1127261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127250#post1127250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's an example step by step of how I think this could be achieved, I'm going to use Science, but it doesn't need to be the only option. It uses Mind 3 / Data 3. Lots of brain hacking (I imagine resistances could be felt as mental firewalls and such <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), I don't think other Spheres would be <i>necessary </i>but Prime and/or Time could help, and it would be great to have ritual helpers:<br /> <br /> 1. You need to discover a very crucial info on vampiric business in the city: Who they are.<br /> <br /> You can do this, for instance, by discovering a careless vampire and hacking her mind trough a street camera, reading her toughts to discover who knows the local faces of the Cam, if the vampire doesn't know that, you can discover who will know. Unless most of the Elyseum never hunt outside their havens this should be easy because of &quot;the social bonds between vampires&quot;. Everyone has an idea about who is who.<br /> <br /> 2. You have to set an unparaleled Correspondence spy net that would be the envy of any NWO agent. You may have to set the Correspondence/Data connections individually, a complex task made possible thanks to your prior research that may take days or weeks, a few Elders that do not leave home or manage to avoid all cameras and other &quot;instruments&quot; of yours may present complications. if you manage this you could put the local Cam to it's knees because...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well RE 1 and 2, use Correspondence 2 (or Data, ideally) and Mind 1 to map out the city area and look for Vampires. If you have sufficient Prime, make a Wonder that does this for you 24/7. Mind 1 boosts your mental capacity to process data, Data 2 lets you map out an area and &quot;see&quot; everything; you just need to have search terms that would bring Vampires to the fore, like superhuman physical feats. Once you find one Vampire you have at least one sect cracked; you just surveil them and add faces to your growing list of Vampires. No need for supreme surveillance networks, NWO style, one VA doing homework would be enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:07:00-07:00","id":1127263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127257#post1127257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain why a True Mage (or a group of True Mages) would have sweet dreams - or would want to have sweet dreams - after casting what you described on a Kindred (or a group of Kindred) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean guilt-wise? Or with regards to fear of discovery and subsequent murder by Vampires?<br /> <br /> - Guilt; anyone who observes the Camarilla and Sabbat is going to find plenty of individuals who thoroughly deserve to be incarcerated. Since that's impossible, killing them is the next best thing. If you have moral qualms, leave those you deem innocent out of your game of illusions; they still see the illusions, but they themselves aren't covered by one. No one's going to kill them, and if they kill others then that's their own choice (manipulated though it may be). Still pretty messed up but I could see someone justifying it.<br /> <br /> - Fear; well you can set up some very good security with Prime and Correspondence, two spheres you need to have to be sleeping while the illusions are going on. Since we have Time, we can have a system that pings intruders and sends an alarm 30 minutes into the past, without too much effort I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-10-2017, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:07:34-07:00","id":1127264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127257#post1127257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain why a True Mage (or a group of True Mages) would have sweet dreams - or would want to have sweet dreams - after casting what you described on a Kindred (or a group of Kindred) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, well, I assumed that any mage trying to do this would be a sick, twisted, danger-addict psycho, who would feel profoundly satisfied with the thought that a lot of vampires are going to be fooled into to killing each other. Well, vampires are pretty evil anyway, so he's doing a service to the comunity, if in a twisted &quot;Hunger Games&quot; sort of way. Who knows?, perhaps even being in danger, if this goes out of hand, fills him with glee","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-10-2017, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:10:33-07:00","id":1127267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127264#post1127264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, well, I assumed that any mage trying to do this would be a sick, twisted, danger-addict psycho (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why did you assume this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:14:36-07:00","id":1127272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127267#post1127267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did you assume this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's committing mass murder of sentient creatures in quite a twisted way. You're tricking them into killing EACHOTHER in a brutal fashion which will leave the survivors with BAD PTSD, survivor's guilt etc.<br /> <br /> I could just about imagine someone NOT being a psycho, but their beliefs would need to be a bit niche; they'd need to view the Camarilla as systematically evil to the point of rationalizing anything bad they did to it. This is assuming that they're not sparing the &quot;good guys&quot; among them.<br /> <br /> So I think psychopathic and immoral (amoral?) Mage is a safe assumption, if not certain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:21:45-07:00","id":1127277,"title":"","content":"Sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well RE 1 and 2, use Correspondence 2 (or Data, ideally) and Mind 1 to map out the city area and look for Vampires. If you have sufficient Prime, make a Wonder that does this for you 24/7. Mind 1 boosts your mental capacity to process data, Data 2 lets you map out an area and &quot;see&quot; everything; you just need to have search terms that would bring Vampires to the fore, like superhuman physical feats. Once you find one Vampire you have at least one sect cracked; you just surveil them and add faces to your growing list of Vampires. No need for supreme surveillance networks, NWO style, one VA doing homework would be enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that would work. Getting that map would imply casting a city wide spell, but it's doable. You may want to establish a stronger connection with your subjects than &quot;a face&quot; in order to trully have their minds on speed dial. The more data you collect, the less successes you need to locate each vamp thoughts, and then to cast the illusions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:25:23-07:00","id":1127280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127277#post1127277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that would work. Getting that map would imply casting a city wide spell, but it's doable. You may want to establish a stronger connection with your subjects than &quot;a face&quot; in order to trully have their minds on speed dial. The more data you collect, the less successes you need to locate each vamp thoughts, and then to cast the illusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if we're using Data then get their faces and scan their smart phone and hack in at the first opportunity. If we're using Correspondence then use Mind to keep your focus on a few things at once and follow all the Vampires back to their havens, at which point you can start scheming to steal links for Correspondence (clothing, minor tools).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:27:26-07:00","id":1127282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127263#post1127263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean guilt-wise? Or with regards to fear of discovery and subsequent murder by Vampires? (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not because of such reasons.<br /> I asked the question in regards to any True Mage having sweet dreams - or wanting to have sweet dreams - after casting what Aleph described on a Kindred, or a group of Kindred. Do you think a True Mage (or a group of True Mages) would have sweet dreams - or would want to have sweet dreams - after casting such Effect(s), or Rote(s), on a group of Kindred (or a single Kindred) ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T16:08:46-07:00","id":1127383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127213#post1127213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difficulty of CONTROLLING a Vampire is +3 or +5. Whammying them with &quot;Kill Eachother&quot; is very very difficult. Vampires have no innate resistance to mental illusions, other than potent Auspex, and the innate Wits + Occult roll that Vampires *may* get to resist Magick depending on your ST (and if you have 0 occult it's no roll at all; can't attempt a Knowledge roll with 0 in the Knowledge, and this reflects your average non-Tremere I'd argue).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry but the Difficulty to &quot;read&quot; or &quot;influence&quot; another with Mind Magick bases the Difficulty off of Willpower, M20 page 519. Vampires are +3/+5 to this. Blasting a Vampire with the psychic assault uses the same Difficulty according to HDYDT (take it or leave it with that book). If a mental illusion does not count as influencing the mind of a Vampire I'm not real sure what does. You are using magic to trick the mind to see what you want it to see.<br /> <br /> Now using Forces as the base for your illusions would get around the Willpower Difficulty for sure. But even scanning the minds of neonate vampires with Mind/Correspondence will be Willpower +3/+5 for the Difficulty.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to simply poke holes in your idea, its a cool concept. I do feel it is much better suited to a Vampire game with the mage as the antagonist than for a Mage game messing with Vampires. Either way the mage will likely end up dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T16:14:52-07:00","id":1127391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127383#post1127383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) Either way the mage will likely end up dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T06:56:06-07:00","id":1127605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry but the Difficulty to &quot;read&quot; or &quot;influence&quot; another with Mind Magick bases the Difficulty off of Willpower, M20 page 519. Vampires are +3/+5 to this. Blasting a Vampire with the psychic assault uses the same Difficulty according to HDYDT (take it or leave it with that book). If a mental illusion does not count as influencing the mind of a Vampire I'm not real sure what does. You are using magic to trick the mind to see what you want it to see.<br /> <br /> Now using Forces as the base for your illusions would get around the Willpower Difficulty for sure. But even scanning the minds of neonate vampires with Mind/Correspondence will be Willpower +3/+5 for the Difficulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. But if the vampire was conscious and unwilling it would be another +3 for a heinous total of +8 (and can resist with willpower and possibly countermagic).<br /> <br /> Wanting to make dracula your bitch it's, under these rules, a good reason to buy those Revised Merits that lower the difficlty of the rolls, like Conditional Magic. Add that to your normal efforts to lower the diff and you will be rolling with a -8 in no time (to null the extra diff and have a -3 on the final diff, if vampires are unaware)<br /> <br /> BTW, I think it's stupid that controling a vampire with Dominate it's +5, but controling a Sidhe with Sovereign or a Mind Master it's &quot;just&quot; +3. Of course, the rules can be easily adapted to protect everyone (if that's your goal), but I resent that they weren't written that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not trying to simply poke holes in your idea, its a cool concept. I do feel it is much better suited to a Vampire game with the mage as the antagonist than for a Mage game messing with Vampires. Either way the mage will likely end up dead. </div> </div> </div>But the question would be, how can you make this character a good antagonist for vampire?. Vampires aren't accustomed to fight this kind of attacks.<br /> <br /> I think that, at least, any supernatural should be able to make a Perception + Conscience roll to notice something it's going on when the mage tampers with their minds at range. Consciense isn't common among vampires but it's a Talent and thus you can allways roll Perception alone. If the rolls succeed, the characters should have a &quot;saving throw&quot; of willpower or countermagic on the grounds thet they can feel the disturbance.<br /> <br /> Then we need a way for vampires to investigate what's happening. Perhaps the Tremere could have knowledge about this kind of attacks, if they aren't controled. And then we need a way to find the mage and counter it's powers. One solution would be to have them seeking the help of Correspondence mages or an Elder with a lot of Auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-11-2017, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T07:17:54-07:00","id":1127615,"title":"","content":"My main gripe with the '<i>Vampires get +3/+5 against mind attacks</i>' rule in M20 is quite simple;<br /> They don't get that +3/+5 against Changelings. Or mind-based shifter gifts. Or Dominate or other Vampire mind-influencing attacks. Or anything else.<br /> Only against True Magick. Because '<i>Vampires are not your bitches</i>'. Right. Nice reason.<br /> Probably sounds logical on some planet out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T07:53:00-07:00","id":1127636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127615#post1127615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main gripe with the '<i>Vampires get +3/+5 against mind attacks</i>' rule in M20 is quite simple;<br /> They don't get that +3/+5 against Changelings. Or mind-based shifter gifts. Or Dominate or other Vampire mind-influencing attacks. Or anything else.<br /> Only against True Magick. Because '<i>Vampires are not your bitches</i>'. Right. Nice reason.<br /> Probably sounds logical on some planet out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in M20 all Mages and Supernaturals get a +3.<br /> <br /> Vampires who possess Dominate get a +5 against all Mind effects.<br /> <br /> My personal house-rule would be that is Dominate gives you a +5 against blatant control (kill him, kill yourself, run outside, drop your weapon), Auspex should give you a +5 against mind-reading and Presence should give you a +5 against emotional control; this spreads out the advantage somewhat instead of Dominate doing EVERYTHING.<br /> <br /> Then state that Mages with Mind are at +5, Fae with Cantrips that command minds, read minds or control emotions get +5 to the respective effects, Werewolves get +5 if they have a Gift that runs along the lines of what they're trying to do...<br /> <br /> Then you can justify it with &quot;Supernatural Creatures are not simple playthings, only Archmages are bullying them with Mind&quot;. I think there's a tendency to protect Vampires because they came first and the world-building started with them; being able to effortlessly mind control Vampires would be a huge deal in the setting. Either that or because the writers like the idea of Vampires being difficult to make your bitch, whereas enslaving and perverting Gaia's servants is an established trope...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T08:08:50-07:00","id":1127643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127636#post1127636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you can justify it with &quot;Supernatural Creatures are not simple playthings, only Archmages are bullying them with Mind&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think Archmages (do you mean the Traditions Archmages?) would be able to &quot;bully&quot; supernatural persons (like the Kindred) and creatures with Mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T08:11:24-07:00","id":1127647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127643#post1127643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think Archmages (do you mean the Traditions Archmages?) would be able to &quot;bully&quot; supernatural persons (like the Kindred) creatures with Mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmages have high enough Arete and enough difficulty modifiers, and can do long enough rituals, that even at difficulty 9 with 5 successes needed they will still be able to condition Vampires to obey them. An Archmage has 6 or more dice while most Mages are stuck around 3, and they can have Archspheres which could make a big difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T08:31:37-07:00","id":1127656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127647#post1127647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) Archmages can do long enough rituals (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>In which M:tA book(s) did you read this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T08:47:43-07:00","id":1127664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In which M:tA book(s) did you read this?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Basics of Revised and M20 have rules about the number of successes you can gather in a ritual, it's related to the amount of Arete, Archmages have high amounts of Arete, thus can do long rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-11-2017, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T09:00:32-07:00","id":1127672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127664#post1127664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Basics of Revised and M20 have rules about the number of successes you can gather in a ritual, it's related to the amount of Arete, Archmages have high amounts of Arete, thus can do long rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maximum length of a ritual I have been told is your Willpower plus Arete in turns, and each turn does make a decent bit of difference. Plus Archmages are more likely to have Cults, Allies etc. who can assist with the rolls. With Willpower 10, Arete 6 and a Cult of 5 you're rolling 11 dice up to 16 times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-11-2017, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T09:16:20-07:00","id":1127682,"title":"","content":"That rule it's from M20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">your Willpower plus Arete in turns</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">. You can roll a number of times equal to Arete + Willpower. Thus, you get 13 rolls with Arete 3, Willpower 10. That's the maximum a starting character can do.<br /> ...<br /> If you have Cult background at 5 you can add 5 successes per roll each time you succed, and if other mages join you can get even more, so it's doable from the start. Keep in mind that for a ritual of this magnitude you can make only one roll each 5 hours of ritual (and your Stamina limmits the amount of hours you can ritual non stop).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you can roll a number of times equal to your Willpower plus Arete, but I wasn't clear enough: You can roll that much, but that doesn't mean that you will be able to roll once per turn. There's a time gap between rolls in<i> ritual casting</i>. If the ritual needs 5 successes or less you can roll once per turn. If the ritual needs 10 successes you can roll only once per hour. If the ritual needs more than 10 successes it's a Great Work, and you can roll only once per each 5 hours...thus, if you plan to roll16 times with a Cult,<i> it will be a <b>long </b>ritual, indeed!</i> (80 hours non stop, but the mages will likely rest each 10 hours or so)<br /> <br /> Probably mind controling a single vampire won't be a Great Work, though, those are for GREAT things. Still being an Archmage helps because you will likely get more successes per roll, thus reaching the goal faster, you may even be able to solve the issue in one roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-11-2017, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T09:31:47-07:00","id":1127689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127682#post1127682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you can roll a number of times equal to your Willpower plus Arete, but I wasn't clear enough: You can roll that much, but that doesn't mean that you will be able to roll once per turn. There's a time gap between rolls in<i> ritual casting</i>. If the ritual needs 5 successes or less you can roll once per turn. If the ritual needs 10 successes you can roll only once per hour. If the ritual needs more than 10 successes it's a Great Work, and you can roll only once per each 5 hours...thus, if you plan to roll16 times with a Cult,<i> it will be a <b>long </b>ritual, indeed!</i> (80 hours non stop, but the mages will likely rest each 10 hours or so)</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I have a dislike for this rule, as IMO how long the rituals take should highly depend on the nature of the ritual, the process involved, and the Epicness of the resulting work - I would much rather make the time each roll takes more dependant on the levels of spheres involved, than successes needed.<br /> <br /> If it's purely based on successes, the Optional Divided Successes Rule makes everything you want to do a day-long ordeal (Hello Revised!), and pushing your stats by a few more points takes just as astoundingly long as tearing a huge, permanent hole between worlds. Which, in my opinion, are two things of vastly different caliber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-11-2017, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T09:46:17-07:00","id":1127693,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a><br /> <br /> \u200bI see your point, but, at the same time I feel that the number of successes you need <i>should </i>depend on how epic it's what you're doing.<br /> <br /> Sphere level does not determine this: What's more epic, Summoning a God or transforming someone into a pig?, because the first one can be done with Spirit 2.<br /> Corr 3 used in conjunction can do pretty epic stuff, arguably greater and more impressive than merely turning into an animal.<br /> <br /> 20 successes it's supposed to be &quot;a Godlike Feat&quot; in the basic rules, it should be something grand and epic.Revised rule for Divided Successes (that's now optional) does not respect this, as the number needed depends on how many &quot;factors&quot; you have rather than on the epicness of the feat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-11-2017, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T09:52:50-07:00","id":1127696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127693#post1127693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">20 successes it's supposed to be &quot;a Godlike Feat&quot; in the basic rules, it should be something grand and epic.Revised rule for Divided Successes (that's now optional) does not respect this, as the number needed depends on how many &quot;factors&quot; you have rather than on the epicness of the feat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Without the Revised/Split-Succeses rule it works - but that rule, as 'optional' as M20 initially states it to be, gets used in so many examples and howtos, it's kind of..schitzophrenic in that regard. An 'optional' rule that gets used in most of the example effect rolls.<br /> <br /> I prefer to go for the 'total successes' default myself, and using *that*, the Ritual rules are okay. And if a mage is really in a pinch, they hopefully have lots of Quintessence to go for the +1-diff-per-roll extended per-turn casting instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T11:25:31-07:00","id":1127718,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> have your questions/concerns been answered at this point? 8 pages is a lot to read through and the last few don't really give any indication on whether you have what information you wanted. The conversation seems to have deviated quite drastically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T12:11:25-07:00","id":1127734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PazuzuAxelf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123364-the-problem-with-flexible-magick?p=1127718#post1127718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> have your questions/concerns been answered at this point? 8 pages is a lot to read through and the last few don't really give any indication on whether you have what information you wanted. The conversation seems to have deviated quite drastically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh certainly, all my OP questions were addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}